{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project","id":459530,"title":"Scion 2.0 (Fan Project)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-27T17:16:08-07:00","id":459530,"title":"Scion 2.0 (Fan Project)","content":"Is this project no longer being updated since the official Scion 2nd Edition is being worked on? We've been running a tabletop for a number of months using some of the changes and we've been hoping to see some revisions to the Purviews.<br /> <br /> Any information would be appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T15:52:03-07:00","id":460453,"title":"","content":"Good evening!<br /> <br /> Updates on the Scion 2.0 (Fan Project) have been exceptionally slow for a few reasons:<b> 1)</b> We have a ton of great material written up, but we have barely been able to playtest it because I am working 70 hour weeks. <b>2)</b> John and Anne asked us to take down some of their material a while back, which was a tremendous setback. <b>3)</b> There was some drama on the forums that caused most of the old posters to leave (I think only Telgar and Ajax hang around these days).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:01:41-07:00","id":463658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=460453#post460453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>3)</b> There was some drama on the forums that caused most of the old posters to leave (I think only Telgar and Ajax hang around these days).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a shame. It's already difficult to find good rewrites of the Scion system, and yours was amazing. I really hope you get the time and passion to continue and that you can overcome this drama problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:36:01-07:00","id":467880,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the update on that! Sorry to hear things have been rough around this project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T14:15:59-07:00","id":468758,"title":"","content":"I hope you can finnish this project in the future but I think you already did a great job. I plan to run a game with your rules in a few weeks and I will tell you how it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T12:49:14-07:00","id":470318,"title":"","content":"We have almost every single purview minus PSPs written up in states between 50 and 75% completetion and it's really heavy school hours and irys work that have hindered pushing things on the site. We are still around though and if you have questions about the house rules we'll happily answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T16:57:04-07:00","id":470481,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think we want to get too pushy..Do it right the first time around, or is it the 2nd time? So if you need more time...? Why is everyone clicking their .38s at me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T10:41:55-07:00","id":471367,"title":"","content":"If you want question here I am : I was reading the health purview and the healing hands boon and it just says you heal or deal damage but not how many damages.<br /> 1 success on the roll heal 1 L/B or it's missing something ?<br /> <br /> You may also want to correct an error in the stamina knack Unbreakable which pre-requisite is itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","user":"Astoril","date":". 04-07-2015, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:19:07-07:00","id":471677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=471367#post471367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want question here I am : I was reading the health purview and the healing hands boon and it just says you heal or deal damage but not how many damages. 1 success on the roll heal 1 L/B or it's missing something ?<br /> <br /> You may also want to correct an error in the stamina knack Unbreakable which pre-requisite is itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed them both! Though Health has some changes in the pipe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T05:32:53-07:00","id":485351,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So I GM'ed an One Shot game using Project 2.0 rules and it feels really great (at least at low level legend 3). Rolls were not as long as usual, rules were fast to teach people who never played scion and most of all I could make fighter character in different way than usual.<br /> <br /> Though I have a few question about the rules :<br /> Have you changed the Tag P ?<br /> What about heavy armor giving the same benefit to dodge and soak DV ?<br /> Does shield add to defense ?<br /> How do you know the skill value for a retainer when he assist you in battle ?<br /> Can aura select the people they affect ? (because some aura are never use if they affect more players than ennemy like Death 2 : Mortal Coil)<br /> And what the range of aura ?<br /> <br /> Anyway thanks for your work I really enjoyed my game thanks to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:03:28-07:00","id":485686,"title":"","content":"Just saw something:<br /> Animal aspect....&quot;<span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-family:Droid Sans\"> You may buy Animal Aspect multiple times, and change between Aspects for 1 Legend as a Miscellaneous action&quot; does that mean that you can only have 1 aspect active at any time?<br /> <br /> Other thing: Animal aspect and animal form: Does this only include &quot;normal&quot; animals or also dragons and if dragons are also included what about animal form what type of abilities can be gained from that. &quot;Just&quot; the claws and flight or something else also?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:12:50-07:00","id":485704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=485351#post485351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for your answer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> So I GM'ed an One Shot game using Project 2.0 rules and it feels really great (at least at low level legend 3). Rolls were not as long as usual, rules were fast to teach people who never played scion and most of all I could make fighter character in different way than usual.<br /> <br /> Though I have a few question about the rules :<br /> Have you changed the Tag P ?<br /> What about heavy armor giving the same benefit to dodge and soak DV ?<br /> Does shield add to defense ?<br /> How do you know the skill value for a retainer when he assist you in battle ?<br /> Can aura select the people they affect ? (because some aura are never use if they affect more players than ennemy like Death 2 : Mortal Coil)<br /> And what the range of aura ?<br /> <br /> Anyway thanks for your work I really enjoyed my game thanks to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Iry can get to the questions I'm not sure on as he's more mechanically inclined but I'll answer what I can!<br /> <br /> 1) We haven't changed Piercing.<br /> 3) Yeah (though Iry might have more to say on this)<br /> 4) Retainers have Dice pools for being Skilled and Unskilled; if the action they perform is using anything but their chosen abilities, then use the Unskilled Dice Pool with a Epic Attribute bonus as if they're a legend below your character.<br /> 5) No, which is the tactical downside of Auras. I wouldn't rule out the ability to make a relic to selectively choose who auras affect, though.<br /> <br /> As for the Animal question: Dragons do count under Animal. We don't see a difference between a mythological animal and a mundane animal. Dragons can give you scales, teeth, flight, claws, and maybe keener senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:56:54-07:00","id":485743,"title":"","content":"Interesting answers and thanks for them.<br /> For the 4) I was thinking of the &quot;assist&quot; action where you can add your skill dot to another character dice pool. In the case of a retainer it seems weird to give 6 or more dice to another character dice pool when the retainer assist him, especially when the retainer owner is only legend 3. Or should retainer count as extra for this particular action ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T04:27:42-07:00","id":489281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=485686#post485686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw something:<br /> Animal aspect....&amp;quot;<span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-family:Droid Sans\"> You may buy Animal Aspect multiple times, and change between Aspects for 1 Legend as a Miscellaneous action&amp;quot; does that mean that you can only have 1 aspect active at any time?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. An Animal Aspect grants a flat +2 bonus to all Attributes of a category (Physical, Mental, or Social). Having two active at once is overkill (and three is right out). Not to mention that those bonuses stack with the ability bonuses of other 3 dot Boons of other Purviews. If you have Animal and War, for example, you can have +2 to Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina from an Animal Aspect, as well as +2 to combat abilities from Warrior Ideal. And these are successes as opposed to dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:59:23-07:00","id":523534,"title":"","content":"Hello all,<br /> My players and I wanted to know how do you deal with multiples actions, especially when you want to combine boons and attacks? One of my players would like to pull out a blazing bow from the fire and shoot an arrow right away.<br /> For what I know, Blazing weapon takes 5 ticks and 4 more ticks to attack (and maybe 5 more ticks to create flames as big as a campfire). Would you make that as multiple actions? If not, what about if we make the Boon action as a reflexive one and shooting an arrow, counting as one action?<br /> <br /> We are a little bit frustrated that battles slow down the whole game... thanks for replying ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T21:52:14-07:00","id":525126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=523534#post523534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players and I wanted to know how do you deal with multiples actions, especially when you want to combine boons and attacks? One of my players would like to pull out a blazing bow from the fire and shoot an arrow right away.<br /> For what I know, Blazing weapon takes 5 ticks and 4 more ticks to attack (and maybe 5 more ticks to create flames as big as a campfire). Would you make that as multiple actions? If not, what about if we make the Boon action as a reflexive one and shooting an arrow, counting as one action?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>You can absolutely draw a blazing bow from a campfire and launch a burning arrow right away!</b><br /> <br /> One of the coolest changes we made from RAW is <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><i>&quot;<b>Multiple Actions:</b> Two nearly simultaneous actions that are resolved with separate dice rolls. Each of these dice rolls subtract two successes from the result to represent the increased difficulty. The first action always resolves before the second action, so you can jump and attack someone at the end of your leap, or transform your body into water then hide beneath a lake.&quot;</i></span> So the badass Fire Scion in your group can activate Blazing Weapon as their first action (Miscellaneous Action - 5 Ticks) and then fire an arrow as their second action. You use the slower of the two speeds just like RAW, so combining Blazing Weapon with a Long Bow would be a total of 6 Ticks, and a Short Bow would be 5 Ticks. Since Blazing Weapon is diceless, you only need to roll the attack with the bow at -2 Successes.<br /> <br /> Now if there was literally no fire around to pull the bow and ammunition from? Then you might need a Miscellaneous Action to get a good fire started as your first action, then pull the blazing weapon out of the the fire as your second action. In that case you would definitely need to wait for your next turn to actually attack.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 05-23-2015, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T06:09:40-07:00","id":525390,"title":"","content":"That's just too awesome for words...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T10:31:31-08:00","id":786791,"title":"","content":"So... any news on Scion 2.0 guys?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T12:36:42-08:00","id":789864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=786791#post786791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... any news on Scion 2.0 guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose we've got some good playtesting under our belt.<br /> And you deserve a holiday present for being so patient.<br /> <br /> Ladies and Gentlemen,<br /> We are here to fulfill your every need when it comes to marching massive armies across the country, standing as a lone champion against another army, and controlling the flow and outcome of battle itself. You can go first in combat -- always, shape your armies into devastating formations, incite everyone into mythical bloodlust, recreate the Trojan Horse, or redefine the rules of warfare completely.<br /> <br /> <b>Seize the battlefield.</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:36px\"><b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/purviews/war\" target=\"_blank\">WAGE WAR!</a></b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T14:09:34-08:00","id":789916,"title":"","content":"We've been absolutely bogged down with life, but we are still marching on. We've gotten a lot of testing into the Heroic Boons of all of the Purviews which are all outlined and designed, but not balanced or proofread. This is the same situation for most of the Pantheon Specific Purviews. <br /> <br /> But, for more of a design commentary on War, we wanted to give both players who wanted to play General, and Warrior to be equally represented. One of the biggest challenges is doing this is to avoid stepping on the toes of Epic Socials and Epic Mentals (In the case of the Generals), and Epic Physicals (In the case of the Warriors). The way we tried to work around these problems was to make Boons that would work in tandem with the Epic Attributes, or give characters access to tools that force people to play along with mythic ideas. Lone Hero (War Seven) is a strong example of this, the Boon gives a War character the capacity to involve a very thematic concept, a champion's duel, or a trial by combat, and forces others to actually partake in this concept.<br /> <br /> I do expect some people will wonder where Riastrad and the original Fury of War have gone. We spent some time trying to figure out what we could do about them, as we felt that they were exceptionally culturally specific to the Tuatha and the Aesir, and some different ideas were batted around. One was make a Rank 4 Boon that each Pantheon had a different version of, with a Theoi player being able to declare an Aristeia, one of the Aesir being able to Berserk, the Tuatha entering the Warp Spasm, but it would be a terrible time balancing these all against each other (and exceptionally problematic if a Pantheon doesn't have a concept to use).<br /> <br /> So, we decided that instead, powers such as Aristeias, the Riastrad, Berserking, and other such concepts would better be represented as Guide Powers. For example, Athena would be a Guide for Diomedes (Ignoring the fact that Diomedes is mortal and shouldn't have Birthrights ect), Odin could give the power to Berserk, and... the Riastrad is sort of difficult as CuChulain managed to do it even as a child, but many of the martial Tuatha could give it.<br /> <br /> We have been using so often that I am more familiar with it than RAW or GBN's War at this point, so I am absolutely sure I have missed some important points to touch on due to this familiarity. If anyone has any questions, ask away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T16:54:31-08:00","id":789982,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/8RxCFgu88jUbe/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Awesome job you guys. Now the War purview finally makes sense and isn't just &quot;huuurrrr duuur hit harder.&quot; The General powers are so cool, I really hope my players choose to invest in it.<br /> <br /> Now, back to translating all of the rules...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:40:50-08:00","id":790376,"title":"","content":"We're looking to release Health, Fertility, or Darkness next. As time changed, we were able to get a lot of playtesting and rule tweaking under our belt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:00:45-08:00","id":790968,"title":"","content":"Aww, I'm disappointed the oriental pantheons (Japan / China) aren't included in the project. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They're pantheons / religions that I find very intriguing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T14:15:34-08:00","id":791086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=790968#post790968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, I'm disappointed the oriental pantheons (Japan / China) aren't included in the project. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They're pantheons / religions that I find very intriguing!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately, the only decent write-ups of any of the Eastern Asian pantheons were on the lost-GSR site, and where Iry's focus on on developing the mechanics, and Watcher and I are tweaking and working on purviews and patheons - East Asia just isn't in the realm of &quot;anytime soon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T22:17:29-08:00","id":792562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=790968#post790968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aww, I'm disappointed the oriental pantheons (Japan / China) aren't included in the project. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They're pantheons / religions that I find very intriguing!</div> </div> </div> </div>We do really hope to write the Amatsukami and the Shen up for our site eventually, hopefully before writing them up before new Pantheons are created. However, I, personally, am woefully under-educated on the subject of both Pantheons, and while there has been some impressive work done by a friend, for our own standards we need to double check everything, and rebalance PsPs, which will take some time.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, the first Pantheon revision has been finished, which does put us closer to working on the Shen and Amatsukami. I hope people enjoy it, and as always if there are any questions, just poke us. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann\" target=\"_blank\"><b>The Tuatha</b></a></span></div> <br /> <br /> The Tuatha de Danann are the first Pantheon we have totally revised from the ground up, setting the basis for our further ones. The Gods of the Pantheon have been completely reassessed, including the demotion of Dian Cecht to being a Lesser God, and all Associated Powers and Skills have been reviewed. If you want to know just why Aengus has Melee, now all you have to do is hover over the association and a mouseover tooltip will explain.<br /> <br /> Eight <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann/the-lesser-tuatha\" target=\"_blank\">Lesser Gods</a> have been added, and given their own page. Including the serial kidnappers of Fand, her daughters, Niamh, Anne, and Clodna. The recently demoted Dian Cecht, and both his children, Airmed and Miach. Also Nechtan, honestly just because I really like his magical well.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann/divine-lands---tuatha\" target=\"_blank\">Cosmology</a> of the Pantheon has been added, including an underground Overworld and an aboveground Underworld. In addition, the Pantheon has been given Six <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann/titans---tuatha-de-danann\" target=\"_blank\">Titans</a> to stand around and lower the property value of Ireland.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the entry section of the Tuatha's section of Companion has also been rewritten under the page of <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann/history-and-culture\" target=\"_blank\">History and Culture</a> which includes an addition quickly detailing several little cultural tidbits which will likely come up in game, ranging from the role of women in the society, the weirdness of marriage, homosexuality, and minor other notes. Oh, it also talks about how to deal with the fact the Major Gods are almost entirely dead!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 12-25-2015, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:43:54-08:00","id":812274,"title":"","content":"Hello folks,<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The <b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/theoi\" target=\"_blank\">Theoi</a></b> </span>are now complete and up on our site. Just like the Tuatha up there, we have revised them from the ground up adding, and removing Major Gods, including the addition of both Pan and Demeter to the list of Legend 12 Gods. All Associated Powers and Skills have been checked out and evaluated, and just as with the Tuatha, if you wonder why we gave anyone what we did, just hover over the Associated Ability or Power and have a little explanation pop up.<br /> <br /> Six <b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/theoi/lesser-gods\" target=\"_blank\">Lesser Gods</a></b> have been added, grabbing the most relevant or interesting from the absolute horde the Theoi have. We really should have more, so, if anyone has a favorite Lesser God they would like to see up there, just let us know and we'll write them up.<br /> <br /> A <b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/theoi/divine-lands\" target=\"_blank\">cosmology</a></b> has been added, but it's Hades and Olympus, it's not exactly rocket science. But, far more than the Tuatha have been given, the Theoi now have a Titan page detailing eighteen different <b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/theoi/titans\" target=\"_blank\">Titans</a></b> who are both allies and enemies of the Pantheon. Or, sometimes neither. Again, like the Lesser Gods, there is an absolute wealth for Theoi Titans, we just added those we felt were most important or interesting.<br /> <br /> Under <b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/theoi/history-and-culture\" target=\"_blank\">History and Culture</a></b>, we present the tale of the creation of the world up to the rule of Zeus, also giving a brief mention to the tricky nature of the Greek Gods Roman sides, and discuss the opposite problem the Tuatha had, that the Theoi are truly immortal, except for three exceptions.<br /> <br /> For what's next, we actually have to go back on our word that Asia is out of the picture for the moment. I am currently working on the Kami (almost said Amatsukami, but as I have learned that's not actually the best name for them) with a huge amount of help from someone here on the forums, I am unsure if they want to be credited yet and if so how, so I'll not say anything at the moment. They do require more research than the Tuatha and the Theoi, mostly because a lot of that research is researching where to find sources to research, but hopefully will be out and kicking in the near future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T00:57:39-08:00","id":812430,"title":"","content":"Yaaaaay for the Greeks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:15:14-08:00","id":812741,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;When Ouranos displeased Rhea by consuming their children&quot; -from the Theoi titans page</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:04:34-08:00","id":812882,"title":"","content":"Good catch Darksol! Snipped that right there and cleaned that up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T22:26:57-08:00","id":813187,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So far I'm liking how your guide to the titans refers to the distinction between Titans and Primordials. Greek Titans were never THAT alien, but their Primordials sure as hell were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T13:03:47-08:00","id":813580,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, the division between the Primordials and the Titans is quite interesting. I really wanted to include more Primordials (Elder-Eros, and Tartarus were who I was specifically aiming for) but past Gaia and Ouranos they are so alien it is hard to represent them within the system. When it is hard to represent one of the Titans, it normally came down to there being very little information about them, such as Pallas. With the Primordials, it was mostly that their concepts were so abstract (Primordial Procreation in the case of Eros) or unclear in detail (Tartarus) that representing them inside the system was difficult.<br /> <br /> I have always felt that Tartarus would be a particularly interesting entity to use in a Scion game, especially working around the fact that he is somehow walled with bronze and has gates so large the Hundred Handed Ones are needed to open them. He has a connection to the Anti-Zeus situation through his son Typhon, but past that he is pretty much literally objectified (locafied?) compared to Ouranos and Gaia. Even Nix gets represented as a somewhat anthropomorphised figure when she makes contact with Zeus before the Titanomachy, but Tartarus just never gets described in such ways.<br /> <br /> The personifications are also a tricky thing to manage, working out when to draw the line between Titan and Lesser God with them is difficult at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T09:50:07-08:00","id":845141,"title":"","content":"Hello there,<br /> <br /> My last scion campaign (with heavy houserules) is ended and my group think about a new campaign using your project rules/content because your rewrite is simply awesome (we have tested a few one shot game with it already).<br /> <br /> So now the big question : any chance to see the 2 purview sky and thunder done so that I could play fully my Thor or Zeus scion character ? Or should I use JSR resources (from an old JSR compendium pdf that I got from the never forgetting internet) instead ?<br /> <br /> As always thanks for your great work !<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T17:16:52-08:00","id":845887,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear you are giving them a try! Please let us know if you have any questions.<br /> <br /> JSR are certainly good people, and they are a great resource to use to fill any holes until we can replace them (especially PSPs). You would not go wrong using their Thunder or Sky. But I think we can do something a little special since you have a brand new game coming up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/c70MYWo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:29:17-07:00","id":846535,"title":"","content":"Thanks in advance for anything you can come up with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T07:28:10-07:00","id":846558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=845141#post845141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So now the big question : any chance to see the 2 purview sky and thunder done so that I could play fully my Thor or Zeus scion character ? Or should I use JSR resources (from an old JSR compendium pdf that I got from the never forgetting internet) instead ?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of, I'm curious to know more about the revised Magic Purview and how it works. The one presented in 1E is extremely difficult to come up with any ideas for. Frankly, I'm surprised they managed to think up 10 ways to manipulate Fate, already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T07:50:05-07:00","id":846565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=846558#post846558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of, I'm curious to know more about the revised Magic Purview and how it works. The one presented in 1E is extremely difficult to come up with any ideas for. Frankly, I'm surprised they managed to think up 10 ways to manipulate Fate, already.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have several ideas currently being playtested that involve Magic and manipulating Fate; though none of them are near being finalized for release. Magic is one of the more finnicky purviews that has changed several times through experiences within a game. One version was too dull, another was too much book-keeping and punishing for players using it. I'm currently observing a personal use of it (through a character I'm playing) and watching it in use as a ST. As Iry is our mechanics guy and the one that every single purview/epic gets pushed through for quality assurance, I'll see if he and Emmet can whip up a more detailed answer than what I've delivered.<br /> <br /> I will say though, that if you have access to JSR's old magic purview, you can't go wrong with using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:13:41-07:00","id":846644,"title":"","content":"At the moment Magic is in the middle of playtesting as Aynie has said, though it has been going really rather well from my point of view as Storyteller. It has been an exceptional tool for relaying information, and I am predicting that as Demigod approaches it will become even more beneficial in that area.<br /> <br /> However, it was a particularly tricky Purview to write due to the initial narrow constraint of \u2018manipulating Fate\u2019 which was already intensely problematic due to different Pantheons having different conceptions of it. From the outline Aynie, Iry, and myself came up with, I ended up writing the Purview twice. The first one lasted about a week before I decided that it left a foul taste in my mouth, and scrapped everything back to the outline of ideas we wrote. Then, I sat down and worked out what Magic \u2018should\u2019 be able to do and came up with the following core to fill out the parts of the Purview we had not outlined.<br /> <br /> Magic\u2019s core is built of three concepts (as are most of our Purviews), Influencing Fate, Influencing Luck, and a final section that is hard to name. We are testing it heavily to try to judge if it belongs in Magic or not, so it may be replaced by something e. In short, they are Boons that allow one to bind people, places, or ideas to be closer to their Pantheon\u2019s conception of \u2018reality\u2019. Due to this being a rather odd idea, I will give an example concept for each concept. These are, of course, prone to change due to Magic still being playtested.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Influencing Fate</b>: Altering people\u2019s existing Fates, with varying degrees of difficulty. This is one of the most problematic things that Magic does, as different Pantheons have different conceptions of Fate. To the Aesir, Fate can not be changed in this way. To the Deva, Fate should hold no sway over them anyways. The way this is being managed is that Pantheons with heavily different ideas of Fate, such as the Aesir and Orisha, have special rules represented by their Pantheon Specific Purviews.<br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Influencing Luck</b>: Blessing another being with good luck in regards to their fortune. Blessed people will come into wealth. One may never create wealth with this, but can bless someone to have wealth in their future. Initially this sort of power did not exist within Magic, but as I continued to work on the Kami (just being proofread through and the PsP evaluated at the moment. All 60 pages of it.) it became evident that many of their figures, especially the Seven Lucky Gods, were effectively using Magic to impart wealth. So, the Purview was reshuffled and the powers added.<br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Pantheon Realty</b>: Binding a Heroic Band together through a Pantheon-Specific ritual such as a blood sharing ceremony if the Magic user is Norse. Depending on which Pantheon the Magic user is from, slightly different benefits exist to this. The Norse example would encourage loyal cooperation, while an Irish version would encourage internal competition within the Band. (Obviously this is based off the old Boon Sacred Band, it has just been touched up to feel more unique.)</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:47:03-07:00","id":846656,"title":"","content":"I see. Thank you for the explanation. Personally, I like the idea of Luck manipulation (imagine a probability generator). Like I said, having a purview designed around altering Fate is kind of awkward, especially for creating spells belonging to it.<br /> <br /> Most of the problem stems from how all the other Purviews seem to cover anything one might consider <i>magical</i> in nature. When I think of Magic, I usually imagine it as being a combination of Chaos, Guardian, Psychopomp, Illusion and Justice. When you split them all into different abilities, there's nothing left for traditional Magic to draw from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:21:06-07:00","id":846703,"title":"","content":"Magic as a Purview is exceptionally tricky specifically due to its name. The Magic Purview isn't actually about magic (and can't really be made into one, as what Magic 'is' can be vastly different culture to culture) and instead has to do with, as you described it, altering or otherwise influencing Fate. This can prove highly confusing to new players who, reasonably, look at the Magic Purview and presume that it allows people to preform magical feats.<br /> <br /> Actual use of magical spells from various Pantheons, as you have said, tend to be from a wide range of different Purviews or even Knacks. Odin's runes for example would range from Mystery, to Death, to Manipulation, and more. The magic wielded by the magicians of the Tuatha de Danann during the Second Battle of Mag Tuired would be expressed through Earth and Fertility (or even an esoteric use of War). When a Pantheon has an especially important and unique 'sort' of magic, such as the Egyptians, it is also a prime candidate for being a Pantheon Specific Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T04:24:29-07:00","id":847009,"title":"","content":"Oh, and Stars, don't forget that. Kind of a massive part of Magic in many interpretations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:02:51-07:00","id":847074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=847009#post847009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and Stars, don't forget that. Kind of a massive part of Magic in many interpretations.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't like to talk about Stars. If there's one purview that isn't making nice, it's Stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:31:08-07:00","id":847237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=847074#post847074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We don't like to talk about Stars. If there's one purview that isn't making nice, it's Stars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So I've seen on the website. May I ask what was wrong with the time-space manipulation version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:08:39-07:00","id":847259,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue with presenting Stars as a Purview which manipulates time and space is those are not concepts the ancient cultures who Scion is based upon prescribed to Stars. Now, in some cultures Stars were used to keep track of the seasons, and some cultures used the stars to navigate, especially when in featureless terrain like deserts and oceans. Despite this, Star Deities are not represented as being capable of altering time, or manipulating space. <br /> <br /> The issues of time are actually rather simple. Our conception of time is Industrial Time, stemming out of the factory work of the industrial revolution. It is broken down into orderly segments to allow individuals to structure their work day. Or, likely more aptly, to allow the factory owners of the early industrial period to structure the work day of their employees. This conception of time is very modern, and divergent from all of the Pantheon's conceptions of time. The most 'Time' you see in many ancient cultures is the Seasons (especially in agricultural societies) and Day and Night. I believe time-travel as an idea only arrives in the industrial era as well, excluding instances of odd-time-flows such as exist in Ryujin's palace or in Irish Otherworlds, both of which have nothing to do with stars in the slightest. <br /> <br /> But, since we are focusing primarily on ancient conceptions of the Purviews (such as our Sun not having powers to do with Fission), the Stars Purview we have cobbled together in an outline has nothing to do with time or space manipulation, as those concepts are modern understandings of concepts Stars were loosely linked with by ancient societies.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue with Stars as a Purview actually is almost zero common ground existing between Stars Deities. The Sun tends to be beautiful and some sort of ideal, the Storm Deity tends to be brash, angry, and good at killing monsters, but the Star Deities are both rare and carry with them no similar capabilities. Short of very simple interactions, such as having a specific star identified as themselves, or placing things in the night sky as a constellation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T15:29:48-07:00","id":847336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=847237#post847237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So I've seen on the website. May I ask what was wrong with the time-space manipulation version?</div> </div> </div> </div>Watcher covered the gist of it. Basically, the timey-wimey stuff of the purview from Scion RAW doesn't fit in with how we view the purviews themselves. We have absolutely no problem with new demigods and gods creating relics, boons, and knacks that reflect modern awareness of science and physics, but those will be / should be on a ST by ST basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:14:32-07:00","id":847492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=847259#post847259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issues of time are actually rather simple. Our conception of time is Industrial Time, stemming out of the factory work of the industrial revolution. It is broken down into orderly segments to allow individuals to structure their work day. Or, likely more aptly, to allow the factory owners of the early industrial period to structure the work day of their employees. This conception of time is very modern, and divergent from all of the Pantheon's conceptions of time. The most 'Time' you see in many ancient cultures is the Seasons (especially in agricultural societies) and Day and Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the Mayans, the Babylonians, the people who built Stonehenge, any number of astronomical arrangements, the Egyptians, the Chinese astrologers, etc. etc. etc. would take massive umbrage that their conception of time was some kind of simplistic Day/Night dichotomy or endless round of seasons to categorize their drudgery. Precise measurements of time are not industrial at all. Many/most of the above (and numerous unstated examples in the et ceteras) had exacting precision in such things. Hell, there's a reason we have 12 hours in two half days and 60 minutes in an hour and it has nothing to do with floor bosses and punching time clocks. And a lot of time in ancient cultures has a lot to do with astronomy. Not that time travel, speeding or slowing down time, acting like you are a OBAFGKM sequence star with flares and sunspots has anything to do with a mythical interpretation of time vis-s-vis the starts, but, despite the folderol in the current Purview, there is a legitimate idea buried in there somewhere. Certainly not in the way it is given and maybe not at all, but it's not out of line. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:50:02-07:00","id":847517,"title":"","content":"Right, a lot of prophecies and rituals deal with the stars being in proper alignment, which is why I suggested that it had some grounds in the traditional Magic collective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T03:17:22-07:00","id":847597,"title":"","content":"Sorry to break the star momentum but I have a question about character creation beginning at legend 2 (case never happenned since we always started character legend 3 before). It is said that you can buy epic and purview up to rank 2 at character creation but can you use those rank 2 epic/boon/knack from it while you are still legend 2 or do you have to wait until you go legend 3 with character advancement ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T12:57:38-07:00","id":847807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=847492#post847492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure the Mayans, the Babylonians, the people who built Stonehenge, any number of astronomical arrangements, the Egyptians, the Chinese astrologers, etc. etc. etc. would take massive umbrage that their conception of time was some kind of simplistic Day/Night dichotomy or endless round of seasons to categorize their drudgery.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a poorly worded sentence, but he was not trying to suggest that those ancient cultures have a simplistic outlook on the passage of time, only to suggest that our widespread idea of space-time as a malleable and bendable thing is pretty modern.<br /> <br /> As he mentioned, it was Industrial Time that contributed heavily to our modern time-discipline; not in depth of complexity but width of exposure. From that we began to see a blossom of people toying with the idea of time (both scientifically and in literature) which leads us to our current conception.<br /> <br /> The most common myths we see about 'time travel' among ancient people is losing years because the home of the gods moves at a much slower speed/sleeping too long/or going to sleep to awaken at some appointed time. For example, the time bubbles of Tir Na nOg (which he mentioned), the Deva heavens moving at a ratio of 1 Day : 100 Years, Taro losing years visiting Ryujin, Kakudmi losing millions of years visiting Brahma, Rip Van Winkle, King Arthur, Geroldseck, the three Tells, etc.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Mayans did have children stories about bouncing forwards and backwards in time like an X-Man. I have a hard time imagining any ancient person not wishing they had the ability to go back and correct a mistake. But we don't have evidence to support it, so we cannot make that leap.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:11:43-07:00","id":847817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=847807#post847807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe the Mayans did have children stories about bouncing forwards and backwards in time like an X-Man. I have a hard time imagining any ancient person not wishing they had the ability to go back and correct a mistake. But we don't have evidence to support it, so we cannot make that leap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on working with Mayans, it seems really unlikely. Since each and every day is all days and all days are each and every day. Or I guess they did since you were never anywhere but &quot;now&quot; and every &quot;now&quot; was this &quot;now&quot;. <br /> <br /> &quot;Will the world end when the Great Sun sets (this current cycle of the calendar round)?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course it will end. Just as it ends every night and is reborn again every morning.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:20:52-07:00","id":847823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=847597#post847597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to break the star momentum but I have a question about character creation beginning at legend 2 (case never happenned since we always started character legend 3 before). It is said that you can buy epic and purview up to rank 2 at character creation but can you use those rank 2 epic/boon/knack from it while you are still legend 2 or do you have to wait until you go legend 3 with character advancement ?</div> </div> </div> </div>At character creation, a player can take the second rank in Purviews and Epic Attributes despite the normal limitation on these being equal to the character's Legend rating minus one. They have entire access to these while you are still Legend 2, but may not buy any more Rank 2 Epic Attributes or Purviews until the character reaches Legend 3.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T13:22:38-07:00","id":847827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=847597#post847597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to break the star momentum but I have a question about character creation beginning at legend 2 (case never happenned since we always started character legend 3 before). It is said that you can buy epic and purview up to rank 2 at character creation but can you use those rank 2 epic/boon/knack from it while you are still legend 2 or do you have to wait until you go legend 3 with character advancement ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you absolutely can use Rank 2 Epics and Purviews even at Legend 2. But the option to get Rank 2 Epics and Purviews is only available at character creation -- so once gameplay starts you, cannot buy Rank 2 again until you reach Legend 3.<br /> <br /> For example -- Mokosits could start the game with Epic Charisa 2 and Epic Perception 1, but he cannot buy Epic Perception 2 until he earns Legend 3. This was done to give new characters more options and diversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T15:11:10-07:00","id":847884,"title":"","content":"Thanks Watcher and Iry for your answer !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:15:27-07:00","id":852805,"title":"","content":"How about Stars having influence over dreams? That's something no other Purview does so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:23:12-07:00","id":854143,"title":"","content":"At the moment, our rendition of the Illusion Purview is including the idea of Dreams. Though it is prone to change until we release it, this helps widen the breath of the Illusion Purview slightly without grossly deviating from the mechanical basis of the Purview. On top of being able to interact with the dreams of others, a Scion who is walking the seldom used path of a Dream Deity could beset others with daydreams altering their perceptions in the waking world to provide a Dream figure a capacity to wield their Dream powers in a normal waking Scene rather than limiting them purely to instances of sleep.<br /> <br /> But, of course, this could all change. We currently have a character using Illusion which is giving us a chance to run it through the gauntlet. Stars has been completely outlined and written, just not properly reviewed and tested. Normally I would talk about what we are doing with a Purview, but Stars is very odd at the moment, and while I feel it is exceptionally neat, could entirely change before we put it out. Since I mentioned it in the &quot;Ask Neall&quot; thread, I will say that one of the ideas is having a withdrawn relationship with your Pantheon is being played with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T19:26:51-08:00","id":1018650,"title":"","content":"Hi guys! How you all doing?<br /> Just passing to ask how are the updates coming on. I've heard you guys were really bogged down earlier this year/late last year, and I'm organizing a new campaign shortly, so I thought I'd ask here which progress you guys've been doing.<br /> Also, this will be my first campaign with Scion 2.0, and I gotta say, I just *LOVE* the new Birthright and Combat system. Just made things so much better.<br /> <br /> By the way, seizing the opportunity, how exactly do the Titans work? I see they are conceptually different than the ones from the books, but are they mechanically different too? Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","user":"Havoc","date":". 12-17-2016, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T20:16:44-08:00","id":1018657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018650#post1018650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys! How you all doing?<br /> <br /> Just passing to ask how are the updates coming on. I've heard you guys were really bogged down earlier this year/late last year, and I'm organizing a new campaign shortly, so I thought I'd ask here which progress you guys've been doing.<br /> <br /> Also, this will be my first campaign with Scion 2.0, and I gotta say, I just *LOVE* the new Birthright and Combat system. Just made things so much better.<br /> <br /> By the way, seizing the opportunity, how exactly do the Titans work? I see they are conceptually different than the ones from the books, but are they mechanically different too? Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello! We are doing well, my final letter of recommendation was sent in today to go along with my MA application, so I am absolutely relieved.<br /> <br /> Things are coming along, slowly, but, coming along. We rewrote the entirety of the Kami in a massive revision, including historical details, cultural notes, revising their entire cosmology, fun stuff. We posted them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/999859-the-kami-revision\">here</a> on the forums, and you can also find a Google Doc <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nn03gHFj_tgASkDPGbI1FgtTBff88OrgioSJzyIvEbY/edit\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> if you prefer that. They have not been moved to the site as of yet, but hopefully will be during winter break. It is just time consuming task to enter in all of the information, especially getting the hover-over text working properly for the Associations.<br /> <br /> We are glad that you enjoy the Birthright and Combat systems! They are Iry's brainchildren, they have made playing, and running Scion so much simpler. Especially when running games online, the one roll attacks speed combat up an incredible amount.<br /> <br /> I could talk a <i>lot</i> about Titans, Titans are a subject I like thinking about, and I have wound up fiddling with them a great deal. I actually just had to pull my God book up from the bookshelf beside me to check what they used to look like in RAW since I didn't think we had changed them much beyond removing the 'Evil' angle. After quickly looking through Ran and Tethys, it looks like you're totally right and we did put some pretty big changes in. I had forgotten about the unique powers, the 'Banned Purviews', and wide access to Purviews.<br /> <br /> Just to save you from my ramblings, what do you specifically want to know? Do you want to know about Titanrealms, their roles in Pantheons, their powers, the death of Titans, or something else? I would be more than happy to talk about all of that, a specific part of it, or something else if you would like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T20:26:52-08:00","id":1018661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018657#post1018657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hello! We are doing well, my final letter of recommendation was sent in today to go along with my MA application, so I am absolutely relieved.<br /> <br /> Things are coming along, slowly, but, coming along. We rewrote the entirety of the Kami in a massive revision, including historical details, cultural notes, revising their entire cosmology, fun stuff. We posted them <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/999859-the-kami-revision&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> on the forums, and you can also find a Google Doc <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nn03gHFj_tgASkDPGbI1FgtTBff88OrgioSJzyIvEbY/edit&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> if you prefer that. They have not been moved to the site as of yet, but hopefully will be during winter break. It is just time consuming task to enter in all of the information, especially getting the hover-over text working properly for the Associations.<br /> <br /> We are glad that you enjoy the Birthright and Combat systems! They are Iry's brainchildren, they have made playing, and running Scion so much simpler. Especially when running games online, the one roll attacks speed combat up an incredible amount.<br /> <br /> I could talk a <i>lot</i> about Titans, Titans are a subject I like thinking about, and I have wound up fiddling with them a great deal. I actually just had to pull my God book up from the bookshelf beside me to check what they used to look like in RAW since I didn't think we had changed them much beyond removing the 'Evil' angle. After quickly looking through Ran and Tethys, it looks like you're totally right and we did put some pretty big changes in. I had forgotten about the unique powers, the 'Banned Purviews', and wide access to Purviews.<br /> <br /> Just to save you from my ramblings, what do you specifically want to know? Do you want to know about Titanrealms, their roles in Pantheons, their powers, the death of Titans, or something else? I would be more than happy to talk about all of that, a specific part of it, or something else if you would like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to know a bit about Titan-God relations, both metaphysical and political. Like are they in an out right war or just two different classes of beings that see things differently? How awkward are family reunions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:50:00-08:00","id":1018687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018661#post1018661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to know a bit about Titan-God relations, both metaphysical and political. Like are they in an out right war or just two different classes of beings that see things differently? How awkward are family reunions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I can totally talk about that! Or answer any other questions anyone has.<br /> <br /> Okay, right, so. I can only talk for myself here, how I run Titans. I know Aynie, and Iry both run them differently, mostly because we have different structures. For example, I have one cosmological metaphysical mess based on rubber sheets and lead balls, while Iry, and Aynie both have their own with their own metaphors. They both are less needlessly complicated than mine, I have had a lot of time to think about this entirely unnecessary topic though which has resulted in mine being a bit arcane.<br /> <br /> However, we have established a common way to note who is a Titan and who is not. Ultimately, the details can vary slightly Pantheon to Pantheon, just like who is a Major God varies slightly. Distance, either from the Pantheon themselves, or from the mortal religious system is the first big note. If someone has a large amount of worship, and 'hang around' their Pantheon a lot, they probably are not a Titan (there are exceptions to this, but being a-social or anti-social are <i>big</i> Titan markers). Being very powerful is a second feature. If you can single-handedly fight the entire Pantheon, or destroy reality absent-mindedly, you are probably a Titan. If you represent a very core cosmological feature, such as being the physical personification of Order, you are probably a Titan (such as Ma'at). Being imprisoned, literally or not, also is a big feature of Titanhood.<br /> <br /> You do not have to be antagonistic to be a Titan, some Titans are friendly, some Lesser Gods are Evil. However, being Antagonistic does tend to make you more Titan-y, especially if you are cast against the well being of reality (such as Apep).<br /> <br /> Now, with that disclaimer, let's talk about my Titans.<br /> <br /> The line between Titan and God is not recognized in-universe for two reasons. Firstly Titan is a Greek concept, and secondly, even the Greeks break the Scion term Titan into two categories, Titan and Primordial. Further, it is more of a spectrum than a binary situation. Ra is <i>exceptionally</i> Titan-like, for example. The only reason Ra would not be represented as a Titan in our games is because Ra is very close to his Pantheon, and his culture's religious system. Some Pantheons have other terms they use, such as the Hittite or Anatolian Gods having the Primeval Gods, but many Pantheons, such as the Teotl, Tuatha, or Aesir, do not.<br /> <br /> Titans tend to have a different outlook on things than Gods do as well, just as you noted. Since most Titans are a-social or anti-social, they normally have very different outlooks on life than Gods do. For example, Bres is anti-social, he resists his duty as king of the tuath, and attempts to conquer his own people when they entirely legitimately depose him and instate a new king in his place. Bres thinks only about Bres, he <i>wants</i> to be king again, with every fiber of his being. He wants to rule like a petty tyrant, forcing people to bow to his rule, and do whatever he wants. On the other side of the coin, Lir is a-social, he withdrew from the world first in anger he was not chosen to rule the tuath, and then withdrew even further when stuck with the overwhelming sorrow of the events of The Children of Lir. Lir can't function much as a person, he is only sorrow for the time being. Hedammu from the Anatolian Pantheon wants to devour <i>everything</i>, having no real capacity to even understand beauty short of knowing he wants to eat it. Namazu from the Kami does none of these things, not really a 'person,' more a terrifyingly powerful animal.<br /> <br /> Due to these various different perspectives, Titans often clash with their Pantheons. Though, most of them are 'dealt with' for the time being, up until the story begins and Scions almost inevitably break things. When the Titans become active again, they begin following their own agendas. Balor returns to his unnamed home somewhere near the Isle of the Glass Tower, and sends out his raiders to raid or institute taxes as they find new peoples. He would likely direct them to Ireland to start with, and then meander around the Otherworldly Islands, possibly down around the european coastline looking to enrich himself. Cronus escapes Tartarus and is picked up by Prometheus who was already on the lamb from Zeus and the pair (along with probably many other Titans) start causing trouble, or trying to find, help, or bring into being The Son of Zeus. Typhon would just b-line Olympus since he is almost biologically programmed to go try to overthrow Zeus (even though he never can, Fate already has a choice for that act, and it's not Typhon). Ran would continue a good relationship with the Aesir, feasts being held, all the while huge oil tankers in the North Sea would be dragged down into the depths, propellers caught on her net.<br /> <br /> However, it is not always bad, not always bloodshed, or world-ending violence. Politics is important, not everything is a fight.<br /> <br /> Just as I said, Ran has an entirely reasonable relationship with the Aesir. The Irish are related to many of their Titans, and both function within the same cultural system, so a Scion of Manannan (specifically chosen because they have no Fomori blood ties, someone with blood relations would be invited in with cheers as long as they had not proven themselves an enemy to the Fomori already) who was a Bard would be invited into Balor's home, just as the Tuatha would invite a Fomori Bard into their own homes. Hecate, Helios, Eos, and Selene are all Titans who are allied with the Theoi, and while they may be... difficult to talk to, being mad, or frightfully powerful, they would be welcome on Olympus. <br /> <br /> The biggest, and most difficult thing for the Pantheons most of the time, as you said, is <i>very</i> awkward family gatherings. It pretty much all comes down to individual relationships. A Tuatha family gathering would involve a lot of shouting, wild accusations, and people getting handsy under the table. But, really, that's not out of the ordinary for the Tuatha. People would die, but, again, normal. It might not even be a Fomori v. Tuatha thing, Lugh and Aengus might just start trying to stab each other to death. There is actually a perpetual family gathering for the Hittite Pantheon, with the Primeval Gods not exactly sealed away, but permanent guests of Allani, the Sun Goddess of the Underworld. Feasts are held, everyone is seemingly alright with the situation.<br /> <br /> However, while I do love politics, it wouldn't last that long for some Titans. If Izanami escaped, things would get bad fast. If Fujin and Raijin's conversion lapsed, things would devolve into violence quickly. If Hahhima returned, the Thousand Gods of Hatti would be in a panic to track down The Sun God again before all of creation froze solid.<br /> <br /> There is one last note that I would make. Titans are powerful, very, very powerful. Normally however this is quite narrow. For example, Bres is beautiful. Bres is more beautiful than a Legend 12 Epic Appearance Deity. Just looking at Bres is not a great idea. Celtic Mythology loves love at first sight (and loves even more love before I even knew you existed) so you might find yourself in love with him, and in a Wasting Sickness. However, Bres is not very physically strong, or smart. In my Titan lists, they have a few Purviews and Epic Attributes listed. Those are ones they should be on par with a Legend 12 God in, if not better. The one that is bolded, in that specific Purview or Epic Attribute, they are leaps and bounds beyond Gods in most cases.<br /> <br /> I think I rambled on here for about an hour, I don't know if I addressed your question exactly. Let me know if you want any more specific details Corax! If you want to know about a specific Pantheon, or specific Titan, I could go into the nitty gritty. And if you have any different questions Havoc, just let me know!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T02:07:06-08:00","id":1018741,"title":"","content":"You gave far than I expected! For me the fine Titan-God line is usually decided by which deities were &quot;personalities&quot; in their myths and who were &quot;personifications.&quot; Which can get tricky with guys like Ra and the entire Incan and Polynesian pantheons.<br /> <br /> You seem to have given the Anatolian gods a lot of thought, do you have any plans on doing a write up on them? How would you link them (if at all) to the Illiad's Troy and the Theoi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 12-18-2016, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T04:57:54-08:00","id":1018777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018657#post1018657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to save you from my ramblings, what do you specifically want to know? Do you want to know about Titanrealms, their roles in Pantheons, their powers, the death of Titans, or something else? I would be more than happy to talk about all of that, a specific part of it, or something else if you would like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to see everything's alright then!<br /> I really want to know about their powers and how they work. I was thinking of fiddling with the Son of Zeus stuff in the future, specifically with Atlas. Since the books said Titans can't have Ultimate Attributes, but Atlas is described as the strongest being ever (which he rightfully is, as I envision) and stuff.<br /> Also, not to stretch this longer than it needs to be, but why are the Hindu Trimurti Gods? (I can see them being, since they aren't really distant and have active roles in the world, but, on the other hand, they are REALLY powerful. Probably the most powerful of any pantheon, since their Legends must be out the roof)<br /> <br /> Also, just wanted to add this since you, Watcher, mentioned it. I play my games online because most of my group is from other states, and because I kinda prefer it too, so Scion 2.0 is a huge improvement to the online treatment. I'm really glad there is a Fate system I don't have to completely dump, or one I don't need a whole journal to keep track of everything. Great work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","user":"Havoc","date":". 12-18-2016, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T08:18:03-08:00","id":1018816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018741#post1018741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to have given the Anatolian gods a lot of thought, do you have any plans on doing a write up on them? How would you link them (if at all) to the Illiad's Troy and the Theoi?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Thousand Gods of Hatti are my current pet project, twenty five pages deep at the moment. I have a whole section set aside to talk about Troy even! However, I actually haven't written that section yet, so I can only talk about my brief knowledge on Troy. It was on the very edge of the Empire, and I don't think it was kept for a very long time. The Thousand Gods of Hatti are still probably mildly offended that the Theoi used it as a playground for a decade though.<br /> <br /> With the Theoi themselves, both Pantheons are quite interesting. Both are Imperial Pantheons, focused on expansionism. The Thousand Gods of Hatti have subsumed numerous Deities of conquered people into themselves, with mass State headed synchronization projects, similarly to what happens with the Gauls and Etruscans, but on a far larger scale. However, the Hittite Empire ends in the same period as the Greek Dark Ages kicking off, so there is not a lot of well detailed cultural contact with the Greeks as much as we get with the Egyptians and Mesopotamians.<br /> <br /> However, there are some features that the Pantheons will find similar. Zeus battling Typhon and Tarhun (I am just using the Hittite name rather than listing all of them, there's several) fighting Illuyanka is a big similar feature the Pantheons might find a connection through. However, Typhon and Illuyanka are very different, one a giant amalgem of animals in a divine form, and the other a... pretty much reasonable person (for Hittite Divinities) who happens to be a giant snake.<br /> <br /> The biggest point of issue would, as almost always, be the Greeks being ethnocentrist dicks about it. They would throw around the term barbarian a few times, possibly boast about sacking Troy even though half of them were fighting to stop that, and they were on orders to quit it. The Thousand Gods of Hatti are <i>really quick</i> to piss off, so things might get out of hand. However, the Thousand Gods of Hatti are pretty accepting, and welcoming to foreign ideas, so if another Pantheon isn't openly hostile to them, there would probably be a good relationship.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Greeks would really not like the Hittite Titan situation. Hittite Myth is essentially just two divine dynasties arguing over who should get to be King of Heaven with everyone else dragged along for the ride. The losers just live in residence with the Underworld Goddess, not a Tartarus situation, just hanging out. Both sides have Gods, Titans, and what would count as Primordials in the Greek mindset on them. It's a bit of a mess, and while just as nicely divided as the Greeks, people are not sticking in their 'God' / 'Titan' camps. Both sides are made of a collection of both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018777#post1018777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad to see everything's alright then!<br /> <br /> I really want to know about their powers and how they work. I was thinking of fiddling with the Son of Zeus stuff in the future, specifically with Atlas. Since the books said Titans can't have Ultimate Attributes, but Atlas is described as the strongest being ever (which he rightfully is, as I envision) and stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, not to stretch this longer than it needs to be, but why are the Hindu Trimurti Gods? (I can see them being, since they aren't really distant and have active roles in the world, but, on the other hand, they are REALLY powerful. Probably the most powerful of any pantheon, since their Legends must be out the roof)<br /> <br /> Also, just wanted to add this since you, Watcher, mentioned it. I play my games online because most of my group is from other states, and because I kinda prefer it too, so Scion 2.0 is a huge improvement to the online treatment. I'm really glad there is a Fate system I don't have to completely dump, or one I don't need a whole journal to keep track of everything. Great work!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I scrapped that Epic Attribute thing. So, I have Titans of Epic Attributes hanging out in there. Atlas is an example of this, he is just primarily an Epic Strength Titan. Aphrodite-Ouranos is primarily Epic Appearance. Other Titans have Epic Attributes as well, but those are the only two who currently have an Epic Attribute as their primary feature. Izanagi has Epic Strength, Prometheus, Epic Stamina, Typhon and Izanami have Epic Appearance (-). The exact mechanical details of this are not really defined, mostly because if you want to go toe to toe with a Titan in one of their areas, you need to be throwing down Avatars and Ultimates which mean there are no dice involved. But, pretty much, you need to have an Ultimate or Avatar, and having a Star Dot Relic on hand would be really helpful.<br /> <br /> Atlas is pretty strong really. The only things I can see beating his strength are beings like Big Turtle from the Wyandot or Ubelluri from the Hittites who are just what Atlas does on an even larger scale. (Ubelluri for example has all of creation built atop him, but he has never noticed the weight of all of the Heavens, Earth, the Seas, the <i>everything</i> upon him he is so strong.<br /> <br /> The Triumuri are incredibly powerful Gods, but as you note, they are so incredibly deeply entwined with their Pantheon, and worshiped on a massive scale. Their colossal power is getting into the realm of the Titanic, but there are some similar beings. Ra only needs to blink and all of creation will end and he will simply start again. Tezcatlipoca causes the end of the world with zero effort, multiple times. In general though, the Deva are functioning at a really high power level. I tend to 'normalize' the Major Gods when they are interacting with some exceptions (I would tip the scale towards someone's specialization, or if they were within their own area of influence, or if they are internally recognized as more powerful than other Gods [so, the Three Kings of the Theoi are really heavy hitters, coupled with their very powerful Relics, the Thunderbolt, the Trident, and the Helm of Darkness.]) So, for example, Lugh, even though the Tuatha are <i>incredibly weak</i> for Gods, could easily go toe to toe with any other Major Warrior God, and if Lugh has his spear, he will win (unless people start throwing Ultimates or Avatars, or have a similarly worded Relic [the wielder will always win, the Irish are weak themselves, but carry with them insanely broken Relics])<br /> <br /> The Triumuri are most certainly Gods though, far too closely bound. <i>Exceptionally</i> powerful though, even in a Pantheon of power houses.<br /> <br /> We're glad you and your play group is going to use 2.0 online! It is not exactly designed for it, but it has certainly been influenced by the fact we all play online through Skype. I can remember playing RAW and a combat taking several sessions just because of all the extra communication you needed in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 12-18-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T10:01:03-08:00","id":1018836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018816#post1018816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Thousand Gods of Hatti are my current pet project, twenty five pages deep at the moment. I have a whole section set aside to talk about Troy even! However, I actually haven't written that section yet, so I can only talk about my brief knowledge on Troy. It was on the very edge of the Empire, and I don't think it was kept for a very long time. The Thousand Gods of Hatti are still probably mildly offended that the Theoi used it as a playground for a decade though.<br /> <br /> With the Theoi themselves, both Pantheons are quite interesting. Both are Imperial Pantheons, focused on expansionism. The Thousand Gods of Hatti have subsumed numerous Deities of conquered people into them