ides are made of a collection of both.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh yeah, I scrapped that Epic Attribute thing. So, I have Titans of Epic Attributes hanging out in there. Atlas is an example of this, he is just primarily an Epic Strength Titan. Aphrodite-Ouranos is primarily Epic Appearance. Other Titans have Epic Attributes as well, but those are the only two who currently have an Epic Attribute as their primary feature. Izanagi has Epic Strength, Prometheus, Epic Stamina, Typhon and Izanami have Epic Appearance (-). The exact mechanical details of this are not really defined, mostly because if you want to go toe to toe with a Titan in one of their areas, you need to be throwing down Avatars and Ultimates which mean there are no dice involved. But, pretty much, you need to have an Ultimate or Avatar, and having a Star Dot Relic on hand would be really helpful.<br /> <br /> Atlas is pretty strong really. The only things I can see beating his strength are beings like Big Turtle from the Wyandot or Ubelluri from the Hittites who are just what Atlas does on an even larger scale. (Ubelluri for example has all of creation built atop him, but he has never noticed the weight of all of the Heavens, Earth, the Seas, the <i>everything</i> upon him he is so strong.<br /> <br /> The Triumuri are incredibly powerful Gods, but as you note, they are so incredibly deeply entwined with their Pantheon, and worshiped on a massive scale. Their colossal power is getting into the realm of the Titanic, but there are some similar beings. Ra only needs to blink and all of creation will end and he will simply start again. Tezcatlipoca causes the end of the world with zero effort, multiple times. In general though, the Deva are functioning at a really high power level. I tend to 'normalize' the Major Gods when they are interacting with some exceptions (I would tip the scale towards someone's specialization, or if they were within their own area of influence, or if they are internally recognized as more powerful than other Gods [so, the Three Kings of the Theoi are really heavy hitters, coupled with their very powerful Relics, the Thunderbolt, the Trident, and the Helm of Darkness.]) So, for example, Lugh, even though the Tuatha are <i>incredibly weak</i> for Gods, could easily go toe to toe with any other Major Warrior God, and if Lugh has his spear, he will win (unless people start throwing Ultimates or Avatars, or have a similarly worded Relic [the wielder will always win, the Irish are weak themselves, but carry with them insanely broken Relics])<br /> <br /> The Triumuri are most certainly Gods though, far too closely bound. <i>Exceptionally</i> powerful though, even in a Pantheon of power houses.<br /> <br /> We're glad you and your play group is going to use 2.0 online! It is not exactly designed for it, but it has certainly been influenced by the fact we all play online through Skype. I can remember playing RAW and a combat taking several sessions just because of all the extra communication you needed in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering my questions, Watcher, it's really nice of you! I guess I know where to ask if anything else comes up. Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T20:06:55-08:00","id":1019022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018650#post1018650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just passing to ask how are the updates coming on. I've heard you guys were really bogged down earlier this year/late last year, and I'm organizing a new campaign shortly, so I thought I'd ask here which progress you guys've been doing.<br /> Also, this will be my first campaign with Scion 2.0, and I gotta say, I just *LOVE* the new Birthright and Combat system. Just made things so much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> The mechanics of Scion 2.0 are something I am really proud of, and I drowned beneath an ocean of spreadsheets when I was balancing everything. Making play smooth, and not breaking KISS unless absolutely necessary were some of the biggest influences in the rewrite. Let me know if you have any questions about the rules.<br /> <br /> With the announcement of Scion 2nd Edition, most of our big mechanical projects have been put on hold until the new edition comes out. So our attention has turned to doing huge pantheon rewrites like the <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann\" target=\"_blank\">Tuatha</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/theoi\" target=\"_blank\">Theoi</a>, and the impressive <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/999859-the-kami-revision\">Kami</a>. Watcher is our head researcher and has been doing an absolutely amazing job with the rewrites. I also want to give a shout out to Sacerdos whose research was an enormous influence on the Kami.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1018650#post1018650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, seizing the opportunity, how exactly do the Titans work? I see they are conceptually different than the ones from the books, but are they mechanically different too? Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>Watcher went into great detail about the Titans, and we run them pretty similar to each other. The important thing is that we do not see the Titans as &quot;Evil&quot;. Instead, we use the term Titan to refer to entities that are so distant or aloof about humanity that they do not consider our feelings. Usually this has nothing to do with malice towards us, but because we are beneath their notice. Sometimes these beings might actually take notice, but their idea of helping would be actively harmful to us.<br /> <br /> Consider Oceanus, the primordial embodiment of the ocean itself. We know that he invites Hera over for some small family gatherings now and then, so he seems sociable on some level. But on a day to day basis he probably does not even think about all the humans who drown at sea or wreck their ships. Even reaching his home (where he is both the ocean itself and someone who can apparently be visited) might be exceptionally lethal simply because of what he is.<br /> <br /> Now, some Titans have personal preferences and goals that are downright murderous to humanity. The infamous Apep would love nothing more than to devour the sun, which is certain to be a no good, lousy, pretty bad thing for humanity. If someone ever put Kagutsuchi back together, he would immediately start turning the rest of the world into cinders, or burn his way into Takamagahara to confront his father.<br /> <br /> But being a Titan doesn't make you Evil. In fact, in a game about so many different cultural beliefs from across the world, what counts as Evil changes from one pantheon to the next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 12-18-2016, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T04:45:41-08:00","id":1019160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1019022#post1019022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you!<br /> <br /> The mechanics of Scion 2.0 are something I am really proud of, and I drowned beneath an ocean of spreadsheets when I was balancing everything. Making play smooth, and not breaking KISS unless absolutely necessary were some of the biggest influences in the rewrite. Let me know if you have any questions about the rules.<br /> <br /> With the announcement of Scion 2nd Edition, most of our big mechanical projects have been put on hold until the new edition comes out. So our attention has turned to doing huge pantheon rewrites like the <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann\" target=\"_blank\">Tuatha</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/theoi\" target=\"_blank\">Theoi</a>, and the impressive <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/999859-the-kami-revision\">Kami</a>. Watcher is our head researcher and has been doing an absolutely amazing job with the rewrites. I also want to give a shout out to Sacerdos whose research was an enormous influence on the Kami.<br /> Watcher went into great detail about the Titans, and we run them pretty similar to each other. The important thing is that we do not see the Titans as &quot;Evil&quot;. Instead, we use the term Titan to refer to entities that are so distant or aloof about humanity that they do not consider our feelings. Usually this has nothing to do with malice towards us, but because we are beneath their notice. Sometimes these beings might actually take notice, but their idea of helping would be actively harmful to us.<br /> <br /> Consider Oceanus, the primordial embodiment of the ocean itself. We know that he invites Hera over for some small family gatherings now and then, so he seems sociable on some level. But on a day to day basis he probably does not even think about all the humans who drown at sea or wreck their ships. Even reaching his home (where he is both the ocean itself and someone who can apparently be visited) might be exceptionally lethal simply because of what he is.<br /> <br /> Now, some Titans have personal preferences and goals that are downright murderous to humanity. The infamous Apep would love nothing more than to devour the sun, which is certain to be a no good, lousy, pretty bad thing for humanity. If someone ever put Kagutsuchi back together, he would immediately start turning the rest of the world into cinders, or burn his way into Takamagahara to confront his father.<br /> <br /> But being a Titan doesn't make you Evil. In fact, in a game about so many different cultural beliefs from across the world, what counts as Evil changes from one pantheon to the next.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see that now, thanks Iry! I never liked the absolute evil thing. I mean, I can never see something as entirely and absolutely evil, so I'm glad you guys left that manicheism behind! =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T11:38:32-08:00","id":1022046,"title":"","content":"Hi guys!<br /> I was reading through the Epic Perception knacks and saw this one<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>SCENT THE TITANIC</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\">Cost: None</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\">Dice Pool: None</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\">Type: Persistent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prerequisite: Scent the Divine</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Just as the Gods have specific scents and sounds depending on from which Pantheon they hail from, the Titans are all too marked by which Titanrealm they have been bound to oh so long ago. The Avatars themselves, and the lesser creatures who have crawled from these deep hidden places of the world all bear these scents and sounds.</span></span><br /> <br /> And then came a list with all the titanrealms and their sensations. However, from what I've seen from the Tuatha, the Theoi, and the Kami, it seems you've done away with the Greater Titans and Titanrealms thingie.<br /> Anyway, thank you beforehand, happy holidays!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","user":"Havoc","date":".  Formatting 12-25-2016, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T12:26:19-08:00","id":1022055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022046#post1022046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys!<br /> I was reading through the Epic Perception knacks and saw this one<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>SCENT THE TITANIC</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\">Cost: None</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\">Dice Pool: None</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\">Type: Persistent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Prerequisite: Scent the Divine</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Just as the Gods have specific scents and sounds depending on from which Pantheon they hail from, the Titans are all too marked by which Titanrealm they have been bound to oh so long ago. The Avatars themselves, and the lesser creatures who have crawled from these deep hidden places of the world all bear these scents and sounds.</span></span><br /> <br /> And then came a list with all the titanrealms and their sensations. However, from what I've seen from the Tuatha, the Theoi, and the Kami, it seems you've done away with the Greater Titans and Titanrealms thingie.<br /> Anyway, thank you beforehand, happy holidays!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah right, the Scent Knacks. They are left over from RAW and Gotham by Night. In our settings, you tend to not need divine senses to notice someone's a Scion. The burning spear, owl head, armor made of obsidian animal hides, those tend to give it away. Theoretically they could be used to help pierce disguises, but then there's the scent disguising knacks, and it becomes a manufactured arms race pretty much.<br /> <br /> Anyways, right. I have axed Greater Titans for the most part. And Titanrealms as well. I found Greater Titans unnecessary, and were altering source mythology without adding any fun to the game, so I cut them. The Greater Titan system also tended to work best with the Titanic Templates, and the general 'union' of a specific Purview's Titans against a specific Pantheon. Since I cut both of these since they were manufactured relations that, once again, did not add fun, and deviated, removing Greater Titans worked.<br /> <br /> Titanrealms were neat, but personally I found they... just did not fit in how I was running things. Firstly, I am a crazy person who is unnecessarily accurate, and most of the Titans are imprisoned in <i>very specific</i> locations that are not Titanrealms. So, for example, Atlas is not imprisoned in a Titanrealm. Izanami is imprisoned in an Underworld. Lir is just crying on a rock somewhere (or in the Land-Under-Wave, which would be a Terra Incognita). Furthermore, their function as locations for God level adventures just did not click with me. Overworlds already worked for that, and when Gods or Titans throw down outside of an Overworld, Titanrealms gave a collateral damage free zone to do so in. Typhon and Zeus could fight without leveling a fourth of Greece. It just didn't work for the way I run things.<br /> <br /> So, yes. Scent the Titanic doesn't actually work like that in my games. I actually have never had someone take it, you tend to know the giant man with one eye, one hand, and one foot is a Fomori, not needing a Knack to let you know they're connected to Balor. If someone wanted to use it, I would suggest having Scent the Titanic give hints as to what Titan a Titanspawn is connected with / related to. So, Cerberus would smell like Typhon and Echidna, both of whom would have unique scents and sounds. (Probably the smell of animals, the mewling of baby creatures, and the distant roars of every animal in creation as a mixture of both)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T12:36:33-08:00","id":1022057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022055#post1022055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah right, the Scent Knacks. They are left over from RAW and Gotham by Night. In our settings, you tend to not need divine senses to notice someone's a Scion. The burning spear, owl head, armor made of obsidian animal hides, those tend to give it away. Theoretically they could be used to help pierce disguises, but then there's the scent disguising knacks, and it becomes a manufactured arms race pretty much.<br /> <br /> Anyways, right. I have axed Greater Titans for the most part. And Titanrealms as well. I found Greater Titans unnecessary, and were altering source mythology without adding any fun to the game, so I cut them. The Greater Titan system also tended to work best with the Titanic Templates, and the general 'union' of a specific Purview's Titans against a specific Pantheon. Since I cut both of these since they were manufactured relations that, once again, did not add fun, and deviated, removing Greater Titans worked.<br /> <br /> Titanrealms were neat, but personally I found they... just did not fit in how I was running things. Firstly, I am a crazy person who is unnecessarily accurate, and most of the Titans are imprisoned in <i>very specific</i> locations that are not Titanrealms. So, for example, Atlas is not imprisoned in a Titanrealm. Izanami is imprisoned in an Underworld. Lir is just crying on a rock somewhere (or in the Land-Under-Wave, which would be a Terra Incognita). Furthermore, their function as locations for God level adventures just did not click with me. Overworlds already worked for that, and when Gods or Titans throw down outside of an Overworld, Titanrealms gave a collateral damage free zone to do so in. Typhon and Zeus could fight without leveling a fourth of Greece. It just didn't work for the way I run things.<br /> <br /> So, yes. Scent the Titanic doesn't actually work like that in my games. I actually have never had someone take it, you tend to know the giant man with one eye, one hand, and one foot is a Fomori, not needing a Knack to let you know they're connected to Balor. If someone wanted to use it, I would suggest having Scent the Titanic give hints as to what Titan a Titanspawn is connected with / related to. So, Cerberus would smell like Typhon and Echidna, both of whom would have unique scents and sounds. (Probably the smell of animals, the mewling of baby creatures, and the distant roars of every animal in creation as a mixture of both)</div> </div> </div> </div>I found the last part interesting. So you've done away with the Titanrealms thing, but the Titanspawn are still, well, spawn of the titans. I wonder what kind of things would come out of Atlas or Aphrodite-Ouranos. Probably more Gods, but maybe something else entirely. The Hesperides are, after all, sometimes called daughters of Atlas.<br /> Well, in any case, thanks again Watcher!<br /> <br /> Oh, that reminds me of one last thing. I probably should post this in other thread, but it's not something big or anything.<br /> So Scion has no masquerade, right? If a frog-headed egyptian god walks down the street, people will know and see that. In RAW, what prevents the Gods from interfering too much with mortals, aside from principles and traditions, was Fatebinding, but you guys took that away too.<br /> So... there isn't really anything in the way of a good old fashioned brawl between Zeus and Thor smashing through the Alps, is there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","user":"Havoc","date":". 12-25-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T13:40:47-08:00","id":1022079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022057#post1022057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found the last part interesting. So you've done away with the Titanrealms thing, but the Titanspawn are still, well, spawn of the titans. I wonder what kind of things would come out of Atlas or Aphrodite-Ouranos. Probably more Gods, but maybe something else entirely. The Hesperides are, after all, sometimes called daughters of Atlas.<br /> Well, in any case, thanks again Watcher!</div> </div> </div> </div>Titanspawn still are... hm. It's a term I use OOC to refer to the... hm. I had never really thought about this. Okay, right, so. Titanspawn in my head are any entity who is close to a Titan. Not all Titans have Titanspawn, Titanspawn are not all evil... Titanspawn are not necessarily spawned by...<br /> <br /> Right, so I'm totally using the term to refer to nothing like it means in RAW. Essentially, in my head, Titanspawn are just things like Cerberus, or Illuyanka's children. Mostly bestial entities that are actually the children of Titans. It's a better taxonomy than just saying 'Monsters' in my head. It's more specific. I wouldn't use the term in-game though, maybe a Scion would coin it, but I can't see the Pantheons adopting it. A Fomori is not a Jotun is not a Cawr for example. A Scion may see them all and go, &quot;Oh, those are all Giants.&quot; but the Pantheons would probably ignore the term, the three groups all being incredibly distinct physically and functionally.<br /> <br /> The children of Titans can be almost anything. Other Titans, Gods, Goddesses, on only one occasion I know of, a Scion. You could have magical animals, or complex 'lesser immortal' sort of entities. Sometimes they serve their parents, other times, well, you get Zeus, Tarhun, Lugh, Odin, Marduk, and their ilk who go around killing their forefathers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022057#post1022057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that reminds me of one last thing. I probably should post this in other thread, but it's not something big or anything.<br /> So Scion has no masquerade, right? If a frog-headed egyptian god walks down the street, people will know and see that. In RAW, what prevents the Gods from interfering too much with mortals, aside from principles and traditions, was Fatebinding, but you guys took that away too.<br /> So... there isn't really anything in the way of a good old fashioned brawl between Zeus and Thor smashing through the Alps, is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>No Masquerade, none at all. Normally our games start with an 'unintentional Masquerade' in effect just to transition through the return of the Gods though. One of the ways I have explained it is the Gods never really intended to withdraw, but by imprisoning, physically or otherwise, a bunch of Titans, Legend was slightly detached from the world. Over time, this resulted in, to use the Greek term, an Age of Iron. To represent this, we do something like, &quot;The Highest Legend accessible while on Earth is 2&quot; so all Gods are forced to assume an Avatar with a Legend rating that low when on Earth. When the seals holding the imprisoned Titans start to break (sometimes caused by a God who wants to be able to flex their might on earth, or Scions messing up, or just time passing) this Legend cap bumps up as Myth starts returning to the world.<br /> <br /> The Gods have stayed away from the world, resulting in this 'unintentional masquerade' (which is not enforced by anyone. The world just forgot Myth and Legend with the sealing of the Titans) for various reasons. The Tuatha are mostly all dead, and more interested in their Otherworlds. The Anunna stopped paying attention to the mud-flesh slave species they created for only a <i>few </i>millennium. The Theoi just prefer to live on Olympus in the wake of Zeus ending the Age of Heroes with the Trojan War, etc. Additionally, the few Gods who have been paying attention tend not to like to assume such low Legend forms, most Pantheons would consider it below them to relinquish so much of their power. And, just as you said, Fatebinding also tends to make the Gods just vaguely uncomfortable with such actions.<br /> <br /> In RAW, Fatebinding actually didn't stop anyone from doing anything it was so insanely weak and underpowered. In our games, Fatebinding does exist, and it has far greater teeth in its mouth. However, it doesn't stop a God from just wandering around a city reminding everyone that they are a God. It is not a punishment, it instead encourages repedative, mythic behavior. Most Gods don't really recognize that they have Fatebindings, past that sometimes they are bound to act out certain stories. Zeus has a ton of bastards because that's his story, even though if he was sensible he would have none due to the Fate hanging over his head.<br /> <br /> Fatebinding doesn't discourage you from being all mighty and divine, it just lets you know that if you establish patterns, those patterns will be with you forever.<br /> <br /> So, once a game kicks off, there is nothing stopping Thor and Zeus to crash through the alps save for Politics. Zeus and Thor fighting would be such a political shit show that it happening is incredibly unlikely. If Zeus got attacked, Kratos and Bia would show up, along with Athena almost immediately, who would have also probably dragged Nike with her. Whichever of the Celestial Twins was out, depending on the time of day, would either rush off to Olympus to bring more help, or shoot down at Thor. Hermes would be dispatched before the fight was even over (since neither of them can kill the other, neither fulfills the Fated function of the other's Fated Slayer) to Asgard demanding some form of compensation even if Zeus started it. Ares might show up, but why bother, he's a terrible War God and not even in Zeus' good books.<br /> <br /> On Thor's side, Heimdall would take one look at the situation, and call for someone to run over to Valhalla if Odin was in residence to shout at him that his kid's fighting a foreign king. If Odin wasn't in, he would send someone to go get Frigg to sit on the throne, work out where Odin or one of the ravens was, and send a message. Odin would probably try to work out how he could take advantage of the situation on his way there in a split second, and Freyr, Tyr, Loki, and maybe Freya would all be dropped off by the Rainbow Bridge to back Thor up. (Always keep in mind, Loki's a giant who is capable of standing up against Heimdall in a physical fight IIRC. He's entirely physically capable.)<br /> <br /> If the Gauls are still kicking around, Cernunnos might pop out of the woods and turn the fight into a three way clash with a half-dead Pantheon backing one side up. If they got anywhere near a Phonecian settlement when tussling around the coast, Ba'al might show up to join in, backed by Anat since Ba'al is incapable of fighting his own battles, and Anat is still quite sore over Carthage. If Ba'al shows up, then Yam might show up to try to pick Ba'al off to become King of the Elohim again. If Ba'al is in danger, Astare might try to round up help for him from the rest of the Pantheon.<br /> <br /> And because of this, <i>no Pantheon</i> actually wants to start a fight. It's too political, it's too much of a mess. There is no Masqurade, and there is nothing to stop Thor and Zeus trying to kill each other, except that neither really has a reason to do so, and actually doing so would just be a mess.<br /> <br /> <i>However</i>, it being a shitshow doesn't actually stop it from ever happening. Ba'al and Yam both appeared downtown in a Moroccan City IIRC to have an argument in one of our games. Only nonsense stupidly good, Arete and assistance stacking rolls prevented a skyscraper tall sea serpent and the King of the Elohim throwing down and undoubtedly leveling the entire city. Deities will poor impulse control, such as the entirety of the Tuatha - Nuada, Ares, Anat, Ishtar, etc, all wouldn't really <i>care</i> about the politics.<br /> <br /> So, nothing is stopping it from happening, short of some Gods, mostly Pantheon Heads, not wanting to deal with the mess that results. More impulsive Deities will likely not be limited by anything if they actually get impassioned about something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 12-25-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T14:21:24-08:00","id":1022090,"title":"","content":"I really don't wanna bog you down with unending questions, but you've raised some of them and I can't help asking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022079#post1022079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Titanspawn are not all evil... Titanspawn are not necessarily spawned by...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably taken with the grey morality Scion 2.0 intends to have, which I really do like, but wouldn't that need to do away with the &quot;Dark Virtues&quot; thingies? (I'm leaning towards doing just that in my games)<br /> <br /> Now, about Fatebinding. Is that part about Fate in the site the fatebinding you mention? Or do you still use the RAW fatebinding system to fatebind people together?<br /> <br /> Also, as the Tuatha [and the Gaul pantheon] are mostly dead, wouldn't that prevent them of siring scions? (Although, IIRC, Lugh fathered Cuchulainn while dead or something, wasn't it?)<br /> <br /> Another thing that came up, not really related, and quite personal from storyteller to storyteller, is what powers the gods. In RAW Scion Lore, they are a sort of mishmash of human creativity and universal forces. In my own games, I personally like the idea of humanity creating the gods to explain things, and they kind of become real, and only &quot;die&quot; when people stop worshipping them. Even then, they might not even really die, but be brought down to eternally roam the earth with reduced Legend. That's how I thought of explaining something like Atlantis at least.<br /> <br /> And also, that gives me thoughts on what power does the Abrahamic religions have, but I already asked too much =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T16:38:37-08:00","id":1022132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022090#post1022090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't wanna bog you down with unending questions, but you've raised some of them and I can't help asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool, I'm on break for the next few days. I'm totally fine answering questions of any sort.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022090#post1022090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably taken with the grey morality Scion 2.0 intends to have, which I really do like, but wouldn't that need to do away with the &quot;Dark Virtues&quot; thingies? (I'm leaning towards doing just that in my games)</div> </div> </div> </div>The four Dark Virtues are actually quite useful to keep around. Except they have nothing to do with Titans. A lot of Titans may have some Dark Virtues, but so do many Gods. For example, Odin probably has Ambition at 5 Dots, Nergal from the Anunna has Malice, same with Tezcatlipoca, Pan and many others have Rapacity. Only Zealotry does not really come up often since Zealotry is exceptionally close to Piety.<br /> <br /> Dark Virtues are pretty much just normal Virtues that can develop. Nothing to do with Titanic Corruption unless it's something like a Titan of Famine inflicting Rapacity on someone. But, that's no different from a Titan of Kingship forcing Order Dots on people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022090#post1022090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, about Fatebinding. Is that part about Fate in the site the fatebinding you mention? Or do you still use the RAW fatebinding system to fatebind people together?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't use the RAW system, I'm talking about the bit on our site. Building up Fatebindings is really nice in that it gives you another resource to tap into. It is also horrible since if you ever need to act against the story you have constructed for yourself, you take a penalty. The penalty stacks, and remains for the entirety of the Story you are in. Furthermore, there are <i>very few</i> ways to add Successes outside of your Epic or Purview Rank, and the penalty is to <i>all</i> of your rolls, and values. If you are a God, and you break a Fate three times, you are at -9 Successes to all actions until the end of the Story.<br /> <br /> This is really dangerous to do, it is a good way to be overwhelmed by rivals, or defeated by enemies. We only elude to it in the Fate section, but there are theoretical 6 Dot Fates which are Fates that can't be broken. For the most part, these are for NPCs or really, really unlucky PCs. For example, Zeus has a Six Dot Fate of, &quot;To Be Overthrown By A Son Who Is A Greater Thunderer Than He.&quot; This Fate lets Zeus channel it against anyone who is trying to overthrow him, or resist his rule who is not The Son of Zeus. However, when The Son of Zeus comes around, Zeus will be, in the end, unable to prevent the cycle of Theoi Kingship from continuing.<br /> <br /> RAW Fatebinding essentially doesn't work. It has been a long time since I actually looked at the math, but I believe it gives out penalties so light with such a short duration they are never relevant to anything. The Fatebound Roles are simple to ignore as well. We do not have any mechanical equivalent of the Fatebound rolls, similar concepts show up just through storytelling. So, for example, a Scion in my game is Fatebound to the daughter of The Lady of The Lake since she consciously forsake her final Grail Test (the test of Lust) to be with the Fairy Princess. This doesn't need any mechanical details past my storyteller notes explaining that she will show up at least once a story, and is in Irish Love (different cultures have different conceptions of love, Irish Love is essentially a very dangerous illness if it is unrequited) with the PC. She also has Athena Fatebound to her in a similar function, but in Greek Love (which means she is crazy about her. Literally.), and then Babd as well in Crow Love (Babd is primarily a big ol' spooksy bird in my games to differentiate the Morgana from each other. So, Babd has been courting the PC like a Crow would).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022090#post1022090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as the Tuatha [and the Gaul pantheon] are mostly dead, wouldn't that prevent them of siring scions? (Although, IIRC, Lugh fathered Cuchulainn while dead or something, wasn't it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Major Gods of the Tuatha I have listed, everyone except Brigid and Manannan mac Lir are super dead. We don't really know much about the Irish afterlife(s) though, so as best as we can work out, leaving them is incredibly easy. Literally, all it seems to take is just walking / sailing home, and you're right as rain. So, the Tuatha have no problem siring Scions, just like Lugh did (though Lugh did sire CuChulain in a very round about, blatantly magical nonsense way. CuChulain was... let's see if I remember. Conceived, Born, Died in Infancy, Conceived, Aborted, Conceived, Born, Lived.) In my games, I explain the reason the Tuatha tend not to interact with Ireland is both because they <i>do</i> have a pact with the Gael that the Gael are the rulers of the surface of Ireland, and the Irish afterlives are so awesome that why would you bother going home to live in your hollow hills?<br /> <br /> The Gauls are a whole other kettle of fish. A few years ago, I actually cemented the way the Gauls work in my head since they are a key plot point in my current game. However, it is so rooted in my own personal mess of cosmology, and most of it is fictional / intentionally left blank outside of God names, and Associations that I couldn't write it up for folks who don't have their primary residency in my brain.<br /> <br /> The short of it is there are three options. The Nemetondevos are alive, The Nemetondevos are dead, and The Nemetondevos have been metaphysically consumed by the Theoi. If they're alive, it's no worries, and they can have Scions normally. If they are dead, having Scions would be difficult, possibly, it's complicated. In the very least, the Nemetondevos probably don't have Scions that often, they're far less... human than the Tuatha. Though, to be fair, the Tuatha are so human it got them killed.<br /> <br /> If the Nemetondevos were consumed metaphysically by the Theoi, having Scions would be a case by case basis. Cernunnos would still be able to, wherever he has been hiding away from the Theoi. He was never subsumed into the Pantheon. Epona could still have Scions since she <i>was</i> subsumed, but not syncronised. Same with the matrona, just less well known than Epona. The rest of them are either so minor that they might actually only be Legend 6-ish, so lost to us that they got consumed by the Theoi, or totally made up and never existed (there is some suspect that Teutates wasn't a God, but a classification of Gods. So, each tribe had their Teutates [which brakes down into Tribe/People God] as a personal patron).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022090#post1022090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that came up, not really related, and quite personal from storyteller to storyteller, is what powers the gods. In RAW Scion Lore, they are a sort of mishmash of human creativity and universal forces. In my own games, I personally like the idea of humanity creating the gods to explain things, and they kind of become real, and only &quot;die&quot; when people stop worshipping them. Even then, they might not even really die, but be brought down to eternally roam the earth with reduced Legend. That's how I thought of explaining something like Atlantis at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm boring so I just make Atlantis the ramblings of a mortal philosopher.<br /> <br /> For what powers the Gods, I just say whatever powers them canonically. So, the Teotl need blood, the Anunna need their Mes (divine writs of authority for a specific area, such as prostitution, war, love, strength, kingship), and some Pantheons need nothing. Belief I scrap since so many Pantheons <i>really</i> don't give a shit about humanity. Humanity are worthless, annoying little gnats. For the Shiunesh, they are servants who must please the Gods least the Gods decide to bring various extinction level events down on their head out of ire. For the Anunna, humanity is literally a slave race created only to serve the Gods. For the Bogovi, humanity is an annoying mistake of creation who really not ought to be encouraged. For the Kami, humans are just the descendants of the Kami. For the Tuatha, humanity are deicidal conquerors from Spain. Many Pantheons didn't care if mortals believed in them or not, the Bogovi would prefer if humanity forgot about them and stopped being annoying. The Tuatha would <i>love</i> if the Sons of Mil were all dead, enslaved, or never existed.<br /> <br /> However, there is... something going on behind the scenes. It's not belief, and no one will ever be able to understand it in universe. When Pantheons are forgotten, when their stories die, and nothing remains, all of reality is rewritten, retconned flawlessly out of existence. No one remembers them, Divinities who interacted with each other never did, <i>everything</i> is rewritten. If new Scions started their own Pantheon somehow, they would stop being Scions, they never were Scions. Every deed of theirs vanishes, and all of reality reorders itself so that this Pantheon has always existed, the deeds of the Scions revised and recast into this new narrative. No one ever knows this happened, and no one ever will.<br /> <br /> A few Gods have theories, they <i>know</i> their version of reality is right. Thoth knows Ra created everything. And yet, in his grand library, deep in his personal chambers, a Venus statue sits to the side of one of his desks amidst piles of notes, tablets, and quills. A small figurine made by mortals who never were, in his world. Never were in <i>any</i> world. A Goddess that is not, and never was. Occasionally he picks it up, and looks at it with an avian eye, wondering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022090#post1022090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also, that gives me thoughts on what power does the Abrahamic religions have, but I already asked too much =P</div> </div> </div> </div>They're around, totally functioning normally. I always take new players aside and make sure they are comfortable with it before hand. I do the same for any neopagans, or practicing members of another religion depicted in the game. They don't show up often, a Saint has been met in my game making his way to Rome for some grand conclave that has been called. All of the Saints have returned, awoken where they were interned, or close by if they were broken into parts, or just at one of them if they had more than one body. The PCs have not looked into it, but they're doing their own thing. Probably a lot of arguing with each other. A lot of arguing.<br /> <br /> I would not allow any Scions. There is... Jesus is a mess. Not because of monotheism or anything, just that he fills different functions in different sects of Christianity, fills an entirely different one in Islam, and is not an entity in Judaism. But, no Scions past Jesus, though depending on where you stand and which day of the week it is he might not be one, and just what he is, is also inconsistent. He's just difficult cosmologically. Angels can have kids, but they turn out as Nephilim, and no one wants them hanging around.<br /> <br /> For the most part, the Abrahamic religions don't take part. Not for any real reason though. Sometimes stories just don't need every Pantheon. The Anunna ignore events a lot. The Deva don't show up in my games often since I know enough to know I don't know enough about them. The Abrahamic religions just do their own thing. I understand why others do it differently, I just do them my own way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 12-25-2016, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T17:17:55-08:00","id":1022142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022132#post1022132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, Zeus has a Six Dot Fate of, &quot;To Be Overthrown By A Son Who Is A Greater Thunderer Than He.&quot; This Fate lets Zeus channel it against anyone who is trying to overthrow him, or resist his rule who is not The Son of Zeus. However, when The Son of Zeus comes around, Zeus will be, in the end, unable to prevent the cycle of Theoi Kingship from continuing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this bit, of the Zeus being overthrown, as well with the Ragnar\u00f6k and any other form of apocalypse really, some of the coolest things to work with.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022132#post1022132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few Gods have theories, they <i>know</i> their version of reality is right. Thoth knows Ra created everything. And yet, in his grand library, deep in his personal chambers, a Venus statue sits to the side of one of his desks amidst piles of notes, tablets, and quills. A small figurine made by mortals who never were, in his world. Never were in <i>any</i> world. A Goddess that is not, and never was. Occasionally he picks it up, and looks at it with an avian eye, wondering.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this right here is what I was thinking of. There is some mention, maybe on the site, maybe on the forums, about that very thing of history rewriting itself to accomodate a pantheon. I don't know if many people work with this, but I'm thinking of using this to make a multi-reality thing. Not in the &quot;multiverse&quot; kind of way, or really too many other realities, I think quantifying this sort of thing ruins the mistery, but it does leave me (and some other knowledge deities) wondering what is &quot;out there&quot;. Definitively going to drop this question on a curious player.<br /> <br /> About the Nementodevos and the whole belief thing, I hadn't really think of that. The Aztecs destroyed the world what, five times? It may not have to do with belief, to be sure. So it is in part belief on the human side, and part cosmic organization. Maybe it's the humanist in me speaking way too loud.<br /> <br /> Also, some players have been toying around with the idea of unification of the Underworlds, and that got me thinking even more about the &quot;outside&quot; things. I'm not even talking Cthulhu, just things so primordial and so basic, like Chaos or the Sky, that they persist in every reality. That was why I was talking about Dream stuff earlier, in my cosmology, imagination would be an important part.<br /> <br /> Oh, one more thing that only now struck me: Pan is dead. But he's still on the list of gods, and the greek gods can't really die, so what's up with that?<br /> <br /> One other thing. The thingie there, &quot;true appearence&quot; as it's called in various boons, what exactly is that? If there was a masquerade, I would assume it would be the appearance of a god behind that 'mantle'. Or is it something to do with the divine appearance? (because heroic scions don't have access to that, even though those are 3rd level boons)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","user":"Havoc","date":". 12-25-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T18:30:13-08:00","id":1022161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022142#post1022142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Nementodevos and the whole belief thing, I hadn't really think of that. The Aztecs destroyed the world what, five times? It may not have to do with belief, to be sure. So it is in part belief on the human side, and part cosmic organization. Maybe it's the humanist in me speaking way too loud.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, yeah. One of the tricky things with Scion, especially for some players, is that humans are little more than animals to many Pantheons. Most of the Pantheons people know well don't actually care all that much about humanity. The Teotl are one of the few Pantheons that actually <i>do</i> care, quite a lot. Not about specific people, and there is a very specific way you need to live, but they're doing it since they want to keep the Fifth Sun going. The Gods survive the end of the sun, but the residents of the world do not. The Gods don't need to be bothered, but they are. They need the blood to help humanity, to let the crops grow, to protect the sun. The Teotl give a damn, but are very controlling about it. They need to, if things deviate too much, and the blood stops flowing, the Teotl can't protect the fifth sun and it all starts over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022142#post1022142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, some players have been toying around with the idea of unification of the Underworlds, and that got me thinking even more about the &quot;outside&quot; things. I'm not even talking Cthulhu, just things so primordial and so basic, like Chaos or the Sky, that they persist in every reality. That was why I was talking about Dream stuff earlier, in my cosmology, imagination would be an important part.</div> </div> </div> </div>A big thing you may want to approach then is differences in imagination. For example, Chaos is pretty much never the same thing. For the Tuatha, Chaos is frenzy on a battlefield, or an unjust king who has failed in his or (rarely) her duties. For the Theoi, Chaos is social disorder, the killing of kings, hubris, and social strife. (Khaos is even weirder. Khaos is just the air that exists outside of Ouranos and Tartaros. Ancient and primordial, but not chaotic, despite the linguistics of it all.) For the Anunna, it is fundamentally linked with waters, chaotic and raging against the will of heaven. For the Netjer, it is opposed by water, which is orderly and predictable, a great evil of the world that must be opposed by the Gods. You could look at how the core concept is twisted, and shaped into different images, sometimes not only wildly different, but in stark opposition to each other. Could be fun.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at core concepts rooted in (or themselves shaping) human imagination, you could look at the Proto-Indo Europeans for the Tuatha, Nemetondevos, Theoi, Aesir, Bogovi, Yazata, Hittites, and Deva (plus several others unwritten). I would warn that the degree to which PIE stuff is an utter mess is great. Absolute mess. But, if you want to deal with the birth of ideas, maybe look in that direction. You would be far braver than myself to open that can of worms.<br /> <br /> You could also look at the cousin Deities, like Lugh, Llew, and Lug. Ba'al, Zeus, Tarhun, Marduk. Ishtar, Aphrodite, Astare + Anat, Shaushka. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022142#post1022142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, one more thing that only now struck me: Pan is dead. But he's still on the list of gods, and the greek gods can't really die, so what's up with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, right. Pan. Pan is really annoying, and really fun. Pan is probably a native, pre-Greek Deity of Arcadia who gets incorporated into the Grecian Pantheon as Hermes's son. Animal features on a Theoi are <i>crazy</i> rare (wings are sort of iconographic shorthand for omnipresent or great speed, not that closely linked with animals), but Pan has them. Pan shows up in early works as a powerful God who is around way before Hermes is born. He single handedly protects Zeus from Typhon in one of the Typhon myths IIRC.<br /> <br /> We are told about Pan's death by Plutarch, which is a totally reasonable thing, except that we also know that the Theoi don't die. The only Greek God to die otherwise is Asclepius, and he dies due to breaking the rules of What Is. He brings back the dead, and Zeus instantly kills him for disrupting the rightful authority of his brother, Hades. This gets a pass since he happened to be mortal when he was killed, born a Scion, and undergoes Apotheosis after he is dead. So, he was not a God when he died, technically. So, we are left with an oddity with Pan's death. The Theoi can't die, but Pan dies. <br /> <br /> There are two options here. Either say Plutarch is lying, or, the more interesting, potentially accurate, and fun option; Pan is not one of the Theoi. Pan is a God from an older Pantheon, and the only Deity who 'survived' (not that the others are dead, just the others were likely mid-Demigod in Legend, and Pan thrived, bumping up to 12 over the years) the coming of the Greeks. He is a member of the Theoi, and he is Hermes' son. He was born, but he also was an independent actor before he was born. It's a fun mess to deal with. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022142#post1022142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing. The thingie there, &quot;true appearence&quot; as it's called in various boons, what exactly is that? If there was a masquerade, I would assume it would be the appearance of a god behind that 'mantle'. Or is it something to do with the divine appearance? (because heroic scions don't have access to that, even though those are 3rd level boons)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I can totally see how that is confusing. In the context of those sentences, that means your actual, physical, core entity. If you have Animal Aspect (Animal 3) and it is represented with antlers, those antlers are absolutely 100% part of your true being. If you ever shapeshift, and revert back to your natural form, you have your antlers. If you hang out with the Yazata and you have some sort of lie-banishing ritual preformed on you, all cosmetic alterations of your body would vanish, such as changes with Unusual Alteration, but your antlers would remain. If you were in the presence of Ma'at, and no lies could exist, your shapeshifted form would revert back to your true appearance, which would include your antlers.<br /> <br /> Essentially, your new features are truly part of you. They are no illusion, or cosmetic alteration. They are now part of your true appearance. If someone used shapeshifting magic on you to remove your antlers, you would no longer be in your true appearance, and things that banish alterations would restore your antlers to you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T19:29:26-08:00","id":1022169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022161#post1022161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big thing you may want to approach then is differences in imagination. For example, Chaos is pretty much never the same thing. For the Tuatha, Chaos is frenzy on a battlefield, or an unjust king who has failed in his or (rarely) her duties. For the Theoi, Chaos is social disorder, the killing of kings, hubris, and social strife. (Khaos is even weirder. Khaos is just the air that exists outside of Ouranos and Tartaros. Ancient and primordial, but not chaotic, despite the linguistics of it all.) For the Anunna, it is fundamentally linked with waters, chaotic and raging against the will of heaven. For the Netjer, it is opposed by water, which is orderly and predictable, a great evil of the world that must be opposed by the Gods. You could look at how the core concept is twisted, and shaped into different images, sometimes not only wildly different, but in stark opposition to each other. Could be fun.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at core concepts rooted in (or themselves shaping) human imagination, you could look at the Proto-Indo Europeans for the Tuatha, Nemetondevos, Theoi, Aesir, Bogovi, Yazata, Hittites, and Deva (plus several others unwritten). I would warn that the degree to which PIE stuff is an utter mess is great. Absolute mess. But, if you want to deal with the birth of ideas, maybe look in that direction. You would be far braver than myself to open that can of worms.<br /> <br /> You could also look at the cousin Deities, like Lugh, Llew, and Lug. Ba'al, Zeus, Tarhun, Marduk. Ishtar, Aphrodite, Astare + Anat, Shaushka.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you mention, with all that unifying talk, I was actually thinking in messing with stuff in the future. Sort of like a divine entropy, the gods clashing to form the least amount of gods possible. But that's only wild speculation anyway.<br /> But yeah, that difference in imagination would be like different faces for the same body. I would search for the core concepts, the unshakable truths: Sky, Earth, Sea, primordial whateverness. The cultural hues would come later, but I'm sure it'll be lots of fun (and research) doing that. Can you recommend any sources in PIE stuff? And any other you might have concerning the more primordial side of mythology (preferably sites or online sources, you see, I'm brazilian, so I can't really buy foreign books without bankrupting myself).<br /> <br /> Also, messing with greek genealogies is becoming one of my hobbies! I've recently been very much into researching the possible successor of Zeus, and everything points to that Zagreus fella, which became Dionysus, who I very much doubt would be too much interested in waging war against Zeus.<br /> <br /> By the way, there's an idea bouncing in my head, what with Pan being from an ancient pantheon and such, about more feral gods. I mean gods from very primal societies, deities &quot;worshipped&quot; in their own way by the animals of the world, like Wolf or Bull. Maybe very, very ancient Titans that failed to appear in any human culture, because they aren't human. I didn't even begin to think about this mechanically speaking, I'm trying to figure out the whole cosmology thing first, but I think it'd be fun to represent primitive deities of sorts that don't really operate in the same frequency the Scions are accostumed to. Sure you might convince Shango not to smash your face after you've done a transgression, but how would you negotiate with the Tiger, the ultimate hunter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T19:44:24-08:00","id":1022174,"title":"","content":"Goddamn, I had a whole post done. Oh well, on to the cliffnotes version.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022161#post1022161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big thing you may want to approach then is differences in imagination. For example, Chaos is pretty much never the same thing. For the Tuatha, Chaos is frenzy on a battlefield, or an unjust king who has failed in his or (rarely) her duties. For the Theoi, Chaos is social disorder, the killing of kings, hubris, and social strife. (Khaos is even weirder. Khaos is just the air that exists outside of Ouranos and Tartaros. Ancient and primordial, but not chaotic, despite the linguistics of it all.) For the Anunna, it is fundamentally linked with waters, chaotic and raging against the will of heaven. For the Netjer, it is opposed by water, which is orderly and predictable, a great evil of the world that must be opposed by the Gods. You could look at how the core concept is twisted, and shaped into different images, sometimes not only wildly different, but in stark opposition to each other. Could be fun.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at core concepts rooted in (or themselves shaping) human imagination, you could look at the Proto-Indo Europeans for the Tuatha, Nemetondevos, Theoi, Aesir, Bogovi, Yazata, Hittites, and Deva (plus several others unwritten). I would warn that the degree to which PIE stuff is an utter mess is great. Absolute mess. But, if you want to deal with the birth of ideas, maybe look in that direction. You would be far braver than myself to open that can of worms.<br /> <br /> You could also look at the cousin Deities, like Lugh, Llew, and Lug. Ba'al, Zeus, Tarhun, Marduk. Ishtar, Aphrodite, Astare + Anat, Shaushka.</div> </div> </div> </div>This difference in conception is something I'm really interested in too, I think I'd present it like different &quot;faces&quot; for the same entity. Maybe I can find some common ground in them and go forth from there. Anyway, proto-stuff is something I can definitively see myself rummaging through within some weeks in with this idea, can you recommend any sources on PIE culture? If you can, I'd be very thankful with sources concerning &quot;titans&quot; from other cultures. (I'd prefer online sources, though; you see, I'm brazilian, so I can't really buy foreign books without bankrupting myself)<br /> Also, with the whole unification theme, I might be looking into some sort of Divine Entropy, with the gods &quot;clashing&quot; to find the least amount of deities and amount to the &quot;ultimate thunder deity&quot;... But I digress. Maybe in the future! (although that sounds really bonkers in retrospect)<br /> <br /> With respect to the whole Pan being from an older pantheon, it made me think of deities from more primal times. I mean, we humans only have been around for what, sixty-or-so millenia? The Earth is far, far older than that. I was thinking of Animal deities. Not gods and goddesses of animals, but Animal Gods, the platonic ideal for which every animal aspire to be, like Wolf and Horse. It's just an idea bouncing in my head for now, I'm still figuring out the whole cosmology business first (and these Titanic shenanigans will only come into play later, but I want to do a buildup starting with echoes in Demigod).<br /> Also, messing with greek genealogies seems to be one of my pastimes recently, since I've been researching about the possible successor of Zeus; which may or may not be Dionysus, I've yet to decide on it. He doesn't seem very interested in waging a war.<br /> <br /> That thing with true appearance, and something I've noticed in RAW, is the level of notoriety of Scions. Like, at first I thought of something more underground, but your power stat is literally &quot;Legend&quot;, people KNOW about all the monster killing stuff? Do the government snuffle that? I'm not really sure which way I'm leaning on this matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T19:45:25-08:00","id":1022175,"title":"","content":"foiled again by my own internet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T20:56:20-08:00","id":1022203,"title":"","content":"No worries about the net problems, I totally understand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022169#post1022169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you recommend any sources in PIE stuff? And any other you might have concerning the more primordial side of mythology (preferably sites or online sources, you see, I'm brazilian, so I can't really buy foreign books without bankrupting myself).</div> </div> </div> </div>PIE is getting into an area where, again, I know enough to know I don't know enough to talk much about it. There is one source which I was sent to by a Professor of mine, but as you mentioned, I have no idea how accessible it would be for you. There might be a scanned version of it somewhere in the depths of the internet, but I don't know of any. It's Jaan Puhvel'S book 'Comparative Mythology.' <br /> <br /> There are a lot of people talking PIE online, and as far as I have been able to tell it is just like reading about the Celts online. Shaped, twisted, and hammered into the shape which fits best within the perspective of the person talking about them. Honestly, even academic PIE stuff is like that, it's all reconstructions, and wild guesswork, but a lot of the online stuff is badly sourced, misunderstands concepts they are building off of, a big mess. <br /> <br /> Primordial Mythology stuff I'm not big into. I don't do the Anthropology side of Myth, at least, I'm not trained in it. I'd say look at Joseph Campbell's stuff. That will be <i>everywhere</i>, especially The Hero With A Thousand Faces. I don't jive well with Campbell, but, that's just my personal opinion, people smarter than myself both agree and disagree with Campbell in different areas. For your idea of a primeval Pantheon stuff, look at <i>The Way of the Animal Powers</i>. I don't know how legitimate it is really, but it's Campbell. Maybe it will be useful. You can probably find copies of his work all over the place on line, it's crazy popular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022169#post1022169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, messing with greek genealogies is becoming one of my hobbies! I've recently been very much into researching the possible successor of Zeus, and everything points to that Zagreus fella, which became Dionysus, who I very much doubt would be too much interested in waging war against Zeus.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's... that other one. Athena's brother. I can't remember his name, I think Gotham By Night talked about him once. I don't think we even have his name left, just a vague allusion to him in a single document. Essentially, there are two 'clauses' of the Fate. A) The Son of Zeus will have Metis for a mother, and B) Will be a greater thunderer than Zeus. Now, in my mind, the best candidate for being The Son of Zeus is no one named in mythology. The best Son of Zeus is a Player Character Scion of Zeus. Getting around the Metis clause is tricky, but she's inside of Zeus, somewhere. Might be a part of Zeus now. Prophecy can be fiddled with on that aspect, non-literal prophecies and all of that.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if someone is Fated to be The Son of Zeus, that's a whole story cycle for you. It's one I really want to run one day, like a Ragnarok Cycle. First bit is Prometheus would be all over that Scion like a dirty shirt. Prometheus is a physical embodiment of Foresight, so he has planned for all of this, possibly since he played the trick on the Theoi with the sacrifices. So, Prometheus will surely be there, showing up, and <i>incredibly</i> gently guiding that little Scion. Not tricking them, you don't need to trick a modern Scion to see the Theoi as problematic.<br /> <br /> Next bit is the Pattern of Secession. When Cronus overthrew Ouranos, he was freed from imprisonment within the caves by his mother so he could castrate his father. In turn, Cronus would imprison his siblings, the Cyclopses (I call them the Primordial Cyclopses to divide them from other ones) and The Hundred Handed Ones. Zeus rebelled, broke the Hundred Handed Ones, and the Primordial Cyclopses out, and they helped him overthrow Cronus along with some treasonous Titans (Hecate, Nix, Selene, Helios, Eos, presumably Prometheus and Epimetheus), and imprisoned the Titans, and later The Giants.<br /> <br /> So, following the pattern, The Son of Zeus will free the Giants and the Titans from Tartarus, who will then ally with the Son of Zeus, who will round up the rest of his generation (other Scions) along with some treasonous Theoi (plus probably Hecate, she turned against Cronus when she noticed which way the wind was blowing. She'll probably turn on Zeus when she sees the same) and overthrow Zeus. (And then imprison the Theoi in Tartarus, which will hurt Gaia for the mistreatment of his family, and The Son of Zeus will, just like his father, grandfather, and great-grandfather before him, be fated to be overthrown by his own son)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022169#post1022169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't seem very interested in waging a war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, there was... that one time. The War in India. I am really shaky on that one, but I'm fairly sure Dionysus started a small inter Pantheon War in India. There was one, I just can't exactly remember what role Dionysus played. Fairly important IIRC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022169#post1022169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, there's an idea bouncing in my head, what with Pan being from an ancient pantheon and such, about more feral gods. I mean gods from very primal societies, deities &quot;worshipped&quot; in their own way by the animals of the world, like Wolf or Bull. Maybe very, very ancient Titans that failed to appear in any human culture, because they aren't human. I didn't even begin to think about this mechanically speaking, I'm trying to figure out the whole cosmology thing first, but I think it'd be fun to represent primitive deities of sorts that don't really operate in the same frequency the Scions are accostumed to. Sure you might convince Shango not to smash your face after you've done a transgression, but how would you negotiate with the Tiger, the ultimate hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022169#post1022169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With respect to the whole Pan being from an older pantheon, it made me think of deities from more primal times. I mean, we humans only have been around for what, sixty-or-so millenia? The Earth is far, far older than that. I was thinking of Animal deities. Not gods and goddesses of animals, but Animal Gods, the platonic ideal for which every animal aspire to be, like Wolf and Horse. It's just an idea bouncing in my head for now, I'm still figuring out the whole cosmology business first (and these Titanic shenanigans will only come into play later, but I want to do a buildup starting with echoes in Demigod).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, if you want to find 'platonic ideal' sort of animal 'Deities,' I do have some actual suggestions. Of course, just what is an 'ideal' is shaped by human's conception of these animals, but there are some groups I could point you towards.<br /> <br /> The Wyandot have an Animal Council for their Pantheon. They are not all fierce, and primal or anything though. Better organized than the Tuatha, really. More stable political organization in the very least. They are, however, what the Wyandot would perceive as the idea of The Wolf or The Eagle, etc. Ashanti Mythology has the stories of Anansi playing tricks on the other animals, that might be of interest to you for this sort of topic.<br /> <br /> Then there are the actual animal Titans. Fenrir, Jormungand, Namazu, and Illuyanka being the ones who leap to mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022169#post1022169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can, I'd be very thankful with sources concerning &quot;titans&quot; from other cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be more than happy to, but what sort of material are you looking for? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022169#post1022169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That thing with true appearance, and something I've noticed in RAW, is the level of notoriety of Scions. Like, at first I thought of something more underground, but your power stat is literally &quot;Legend&quot;, people KNOW about all the monster killing stuff? Do the government snuffle that? I'm not really sure which way I'm leaning on this matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I normally rule it that people know. Legend 2 is small, maybe you're a little local hero, nothing quite overtly supernatural. By Legend 4, you are probably on international news. By Demigod, a Social Scion who felt like it could declare themselves King of America and get away with it. Initially, governments will panic. Well, some. I don't think India would. Again, I don't know too much about Hinduism past some colonial period stuff, but a Deva Scion running around in India would have an absolute ton of public support. The States might try to cover it up or control Scions, but that would... be very hard. Especially up against the Mental and Social Scions. Even at Hero, they're scary for States. Canada would probably just get mildly concerned about it, but if it was in the public eye (which Scions will be) it would probably be a public safety situation which a smart Scion can easily turn to their side. The EU wouldn't be able to react quickly enough, except France who just ignores the rules when they're inconvenient. But, the French have a dead Pantheon, so if Scions started cropping up, it probably wouldn't be too much of an issue for them.<br /> <br /> States might try for the cover up, but it wouldn't last long. And, on top of that, different States would react differently. A Bogovi Scion in Russia would be an utter mess due to just like every front of that situation being a mess. A Tuatha Scion in Ireland <i>should</i> concern the Irish, but it probably wouldn't. By the time a Scion is Legend 3, covering them up would be impossible. You could kill them, but you gotta hope you're not killing the kid of a vindictive, or family oriented Pantheon. Kill Telipinu's Scion and your entire State will go full famine mode, nothing growing, birth rate for humans and animals would go to zero, everyone would be lethargic, and starving to death. Kill Marduk's kid and your capital city would suddenly have a case of a very pissed off Marduk shouting about how you're all ants, and he's going to kill your king even if you explain you don't have one. Kill Huitz's kid and you're going to have a terrible day...<br /> <br /> Really, actually, a State killing a Scion would be a great opening for a story. It would cause an absolute shitshow, and would be a great way to just have a snap-to return of the Divine. Everything's normal, and then a black ops team kills a woman who had a burning spear, a great white hound with red ears, and was making everyone who she talked to fall in love with her. Next morning an irate Lugh is in your capital building demanding a honor price with his Spear of Victory in his hand, entirely capable of fighting the entirety of your armed forces and winning with minimal effort. The Morgana would be hanging around in the back of the room. And that's with the Tuatha. Kill Poseidon's kid, and Oklahoma is suddenly under water.<br /> <br /> Hmm... I'm going to use that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T05:21:41-08:00","id":1022280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022203#post1022203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries about the net problems, I totally understand.<br /> PIE is getting into an area where, again, I know enough to know I don't know enough to talk much about it. There is one source which I was sent to by a Professor of mine, but as you mentioned, I have no idea how accessible it would be for you. There might be a scanned version of it somewhere in the depths of the internet, but I don't know of any. It's Jaan Puhvel'S book 'Comparative Mythology.'<br /> <br /> There are a lot of people talking PIE online, and as far as I have been able to tell it is just like reading about the Celts online. Shaped, twisted, and hammered into the shape which fits best within the perspective of the person talking about them. Honestly, even academic PIE stuff is like that, it's all reconstructions, and wild guesswork, but a lot of the online stuff is badly sourced, misunderstands concepts they are building off of, a big mess.<br /> <br /> Primordial Mythology stuff I'm not big into. I don't do the Anthropology side of Myth, at least, I'm not trained in it. I'd say look at Joseph Campbell's stuff. That will be <i>everywhere</i>, especially The Hero With A Thousand Faces. I don't jive well with Campbell, but, that's just my personal opinion, people smarter than myself both agree and disagree with Campbell in different areas. For your idea of a primeval Pantheon stuff, look at <i>The Way of the Animal Powers</i>. I don't know how legitimate it is really, but it's Campbell. Maybe it will be useful. You can probably find copies of his work all over the place on line, it's crazy popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just might look into that, thanks! I've already heard about Campbell's stuff, haven't got around to reading it though. And about the primordial pantheon thingies, I might simplify that a bit in my games. Not only I don't wanna have to get a degree to run a game, but also most of my players don't even care too much about mythology per se. They like it when it's presented to them, but overall indifferent, so I don't want to fucks too much on this too.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022203#post1022203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best Son of Zeus is a Player Character Scion of Zeus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I really wanted to run the story and trajectory of a Thunderer, but as amazing as it sounds, no player got interested in being a son or daughter of Zeus, and I'm not sure if I want to put an allied NPC there just to do this. Either it's fun, or it takes too much of the limelight away from the player characters. It might, however, be a preferable solution to &quot;Dionysus suddenly decided he wants to press his claim on Mt. Olympus&quot;. (The thing about the war in India, I have to look deeper into that, this is about the fifth time I hear it mentioned)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022203#post1022203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyandot have an Animal Council for their Pantheon. They are not all fierce, and primal or anything though. Better organized than the Tuatha, really. More stable political organization in the very least. They are, however, what the Wyandot would perceive as the idea of The Wolf or The Eagle, etc. Ashanti Mythology has the stories of Anansi playing tricks on the other animals, that might be of interest to you for this sort of topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this very interesting as a basis or precedence for what I want to do. In retrospect, I'm pretty sure this &quot;Primordial-Animal-Deity&quot; thing came about when I was reading on Werewolf: the Forsaken, the whole Father Wolf debacle. But I don't want to base something on ficctional religions.<br /> And I've read about Anansi, only superficially though. I think Neil Gaiman has a book about it, it's called Anansi Boys, I stumbled on it while searching for the english name for Stardust. Very interesting story, and on the spirit of what I was thinking of doing.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022203#post1022203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be more than happy to, but what sort of material are you looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things about the Aztec Titans, or the closest they have to them. The Tuatha, Theoi, and Kami you already covered, and I already have my own conception of the Aesir and Netjer Titans, but I just can't see the &quot;Teotl&quot; Titans, what with the whole world destroying stuff. Also, the Orisha Titans. I've brushed about a lot with the Orisha on my daily life, as Candombl\u00e9 is a very popular brazilian religion based on them, but I never delved too deeply on them. Their creation myth already begins with &quot;There was a sky and the sea, and then the Gods thought they needed land [...]&quot;, no mention of Primordials of any kind. Also, the Tuatha don't have them too, their story is even somewhat Abrahamic in it's start, what with Cessair and such.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022203#post1022203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, actually, a State killing a Scion would be a great opening for a story. It would cause an absolute shitshow, and would be a great way to just have a snap-to return of the Divine. Everything's normal, and then a black ops team kills a woman who had a burning spear, a great white hound with red ears, and was making everyone who she talked to fall in love with her. Next morning an irate Lugh is in your capital building demanding a honor price with his Spear of Victory in his hand, entirely capable of fighting the entirety of your armed forces and winning with minimal effort. The Morgana would be hanging around in the back of the room. And that's with the Tuatha. Kill Poseidon's kid, and Oklahoma is suddenly under water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I want to do this now.<br /> But really, this is a good way to show the Scions how much they matter. After all, that is one of the weird things to wrap your head around in Scion: the Gods don't really care too much about humans, so you figure they won't care too much about you, but you're not human anymore, you're part of the family. And most of my players (maybe this is Percy Jackson's fault) almost always start the game thinking there is some sort of whole society of Scions behind the scenes and stuff, but I like to think there are about, what, about 20 Scions running around the world, so the death of one REALLY is something of concern to the gods. (Even the distant ones of the Anunna)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T10:11:44-08:00","id":1022383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022280#post1022280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things about the Aztec Titans, or the closest they have to them. The Tuatha, Theoi, and Kami you already covered, and I already have my own conception of the Aesir and Netjer Titans, but I just can't see the &quot;Teotl&quot; Titans, what with the whole world destroying stuff. Also, the Orisha Titans. I've brushed about a lot with the Orisha on my daily life, as Candombl\u00e9 is a very popular brazilian religion based on them, but I never delved too deeply on them. Their creation myth already begins with &quot;There was a sky and the sea, and then the Gods thought they needed land [...]&quot;, no mention of Primordials of any kind. Also, the Tuatha don't have them too, their story is even somewhat Abrahamic in it's start, what with Cessair and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orisha Titans is something I unfortunately know nothing about, but I can talk about Teotl Titans. This is all drawn from conversation with my friend Griffinguy24, he knows Central and South American Mythology way better than I do. But, we put together a list. Ometeotl, Itzpapalotl, Mixcotal, Coyolzauhqui, Coatlicue, Cipactli, Chantico, Malinalxochitl, and my favorite, Itzlacoliuhqui. If you are looking to divide them up into Titans and Primordials as Scion 2e is looking to do, I couldn't make many suggestions except Ometeotl and Cipactli are good Promordials. I just don't know enough about the others to give any advice. I do have a good book I can give you access to for the Aztects actually. I just have to nip out for a few hours, but when I'm back I can PM it to yourself.<br /> <br /> The start of the Tuatha myths is literally a localized rip of the Book of Genesis, goes on for ages. Then you get the actual invasions of Ireland coming through. If you wanted to get some Tuatha Primordials, there... hm. Lir, and Danu I would both make Primordials. Fintan mac Bochra I would also list alongside them. Cessair, Partholon, and Nemed are also all options, just because they are dead shouldn't discount them from being a Primordial in the context of the Tuatha. If being dead discounts someone, both their Titan and God lists are gutted. <br /> <br /> I would be tempted to make Mil Espaine a Primordial of some sort. Banba, Fodla, Eriu, along with Mac Cuill, Mac Cecht, and Mac Greine are also strong options for Primordial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022280#post1022280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, this is a good way to show the Scions how much they matter. After all, that is one of the weird things to wrap your head around in Scion: the Gods don't really care too much about humans, so you figure they won't care too much about you, but you're not human anymore, you're part of the family. And most of my players (maybe this is Percy Jackson's fault) almost always start the game thinking there is some sort of whole society of Scions behind the scenes and stuff, but I like to think there are about, what, about 20 Scions running around the world, so the death of one REALLY is something of concern to the gods. (Even the distant ones of the Anunna)</div> </div> </div> </div>Being family is big, and the other big aspect of it is that, even if a Deity doesn't care about their Scions, killing one of their Scions is an insult. Kill a Theoi kid, and you've acted against the Gods probably. Act against the kids of one of the Three Kings and you've directly worked against the will of the Gods. While the Anunna for example may not care a ton about their kids personally, they would be <i>aghast</i> if mortals <i>dared</i> to challenge them by slaying one of their children. It would be a direct insult to them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T10:52:15-08:00","id":1022391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022383#post1022383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a good book I can give you access to for the Aztects actually. I just have to nip out for a few hours, but when I'm back I can PM it to yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do!<br /> <br /> I think Lir and Danu are the best suited Primordials for the Tuatha. The others, while very important, are more akin to my conception of Titan.<br /> <br /> In any case, thanks a lot! This has been of great help!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4533-havoc","name":"Havoc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T11:58:56-08:00","id":1022878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022383#post1022383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orisha Titans is something I unfortunately know nothing about</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Havoc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/459530-scion-2-0-fan-project?p=1022280#post1022280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Orisha Titans. I've brushed about a lot with the Orisha on my daily life, as Candombl\u00e9 is a very popular brazilian religion based on them, but I never delved too deeply on them. Their creation myth already begins with &quot;There was a sky and the sea, and then the Gods thought they needed land [...]&quot;, no mention of Primordials of any kind. Also, the Tuatha don't have them too, their story is even somewhat Abrahamic in it's start, what with Cessair and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Orisha Titans as such, if I may chime in, are a difficult issue. I think it was mentioned that 2E was not gonna have any at all, which does kinda make sense, but is not without alternative.<br /> <br /> Basically, Yoruba cosmology as we know it doesn't really leave space for any Primordial but the High God Olorun/Olodumare, the &quot;Owner of Heaven&quot;. What his standing before the arrival of Abrahamic influence actually was is hard to say, but today he is actually the only &quot;true&quot; God of the Yoruba - the Orisha themselves could be compared to the Persian Yazata or Buddhist Bodhisattvas in their role as god-like spiritual beings below the &quot;true&quot; God. Olorun is definitely a creator in as far as he created the first Orisha, and ordered them to make the world. He also participates in the creation of new humans, blowing life into the forms fashioned by Obatala. Otherwise, he is depicted as a mostly withdrawn deity who is not prayed to, and only acts in myths when challenged - a perfect Primordial, really. But it is interesting at least that there are beings who think they can challenge him, so let's have a look at them as well.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, both of them think they can stand up to Olorun because they believe to be as old or older than he is, showing that they, too, arose at the beginning of time. The first of these is the Earth Goddess. She seems to be mostly called by her Fon/Dahomey name of Nana Buruku. You may sometimes find her named Onile as well, but some scholars seem to think that is more properly only the name of a certain ritual implement. In any case, the Earth Goddess is an interesting case. While she has more cult presence than most figures we would consider Titans and Primordials, those are mostly mystery cults and secret societies - the Earth Goddess is a deity of justice, who is closely connected to the exclusive and secretive Ogboni Society, which administrates such judicial duties in most Yoruba communities. In fact, the whole reasoning for why crimes must be punished is because they <i>soil the Earth</i>. And as an old, motherly goddess, the Earth Goddess is also connected to Yoruba witches, which are also very much concerned with justice (I previously talked about them here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=999592#post999592\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...592#post999592</a> ).<br /> The most famous myth about the Earth Goddess is the one about her contendings with Olorun (there are different versions of the myth, of course, I'll just cite the one I know best): Olorun and the Earth Goddess go hunting together, but they only catch a single rat. They then begin argueing over who should keep the rat, each claiming the right of seniority. In the end, Olorun angrily lets the Earth Goddess keep the rat, but he withholds rain from her in return. Soon parched, the Earth Goddess begs forgiveness, and sends the rat to Olorun carried by a vulture (or the goddess Oshun in the shape of a vulture). Thereupon, Olorun lets the rains return, and it rains so mightily that the feathers on the vulture's head fall out from it.<br /> Thus, I'd say the Earth Goddess would make a very interesting Primordial or Titan, as long as one keeps in mind that she's still inferior to Olorun.<br /> <br /> The second, more difficult case of contending with Olorun would be the sea deity Olokun, whose sometimes depicted as male, and sometimes as female. Olokun has a very lively cult and many myths, and is most often, like most Orisha, called a child of Yemoja, but there are some accounts of Olokun being in fact the primordial sea on which the Earth was created, thus a being almost as old as Olorun. Olokun is a destructive deity which needed to be bound in golden chains to keep them from constantly flooding the earth - and the reason for this wrath is, again, Olokun's haughty assumption that they are as old and powerful as Olorun himself. Instead of going hunting, however, Olokun challenged Olorun to a weaving contest, but Olorun just sent his lowly messenger, the chamaeleon. Soon, Olokun was utterly devastated, for this simple creature, not even the master they challenged himself, could with its skin best even the most wonderful of Olokun's creations. So this deity as well was humbled.<br /> The apparent age of Olokun and the necessity of binding them seem to make a strong case for a Titan, but in light of the very strong cult of the deity, and their many more positive appearances in myth, I would personally prefer them as a deity.<br /> <br /> Then, there are some other figures like Shopona/Babalu Aye, Yemoja, Osanyin, and so on, who are all either very old, or vaguely antagonistic, or both, but none of them reach the level of the figures named above, and all of them have large cults. You could make them Titans, GBN did, for a fact, but I for my part wouldn't. The only other one I can think of is the rainbow serpent Oshumare, which is very little worshipped, and sometimes described as an ancient, ever rejuvenating being hidden deep in the forest. A little outside this whole scheme is another group then, who for their otherness and inevitability might be Titans after all, the 201 Aganju, &quot;the Warriors&quot;, demons opposite the godly Orisha, who personify such concepts as death (&quot;Iku&quot;), pestilence (&quot;Arun&quot;), and so on. The only one of them who goes mentioned in a myth or two of his one is Iku, the hammer-wielding spirit of death, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}